{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n \"''^- '\"\\\\[ \\\\]\\\" docs/BACKLOG.md | sed -n '1,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"42:- [ ] Integrate signed provenance and trust tiers into candidate planning and activation policy.\n48:- [ ] Replace shared Luau service globals with generation-stamped, Rust-owned, capability-filtered context state.\n49:- [ ] Make service methods correlated awaitable transactions with call IDs, deadlines, cancellation, and terminal outcomes.\n50:- [ ] Make optimistic state writes settle or roll back transactionally without overriding newer writes.\n51:- [ ] Compile and enforce explicit read, event-subscription, and per-method operation policy at every service boundary.\n52:- [ ] Replace additive registry mutation with one immutable generation-stamped resolved service catalog.\n53:- [ ] Compile recursive named/array/optional/result schemas and enforce them for state, events, inputs, and outputs.\n54:- [ ] Prepare provider output and commit provider selection only after validated readiness and initial state.\n55:- [ ] Deliver generation-stamped availability transitions and reject stale state, event, and result messages.\n56:- [ ] Diff executable consumer/provider contracts in both directions, including external candidate contracts and behavioral annotations.\n57:- [ ] Canonicalize contract identities and make graph, runtime, LSP, codegen, docs, and diagnostics consume one compiled artifact.\n58:- [ ] Remove the transitional service registry after remaining callers migrate to the generation-stamped catalog.\n59:- [ ] Introduce an immutable compiled contract containing schemas, operation policy, fingerprints, and declaration provenance.\n60:- [ ] Generate Luau consumer types, provider stubs, mocks, and contract documentation from compiled contracts.\n61:- [ ] Model optional service feature groups explicitly and negotiate them per provider, or remove the unsupported claim.\n62:- [ ] Make consumer/provider compatibility classifications independently expressible rather than using one undirected label.\n63:- [ ] Use one call transaction model for awaitable results, cancellation, deadlines, coalescing, tracing, and optimistic rollback.\n69:- [ ] Build the theme catalog only from graph-authorized descriptors with scoped ownership, modes, and contained source handles.\n70:- [ ] Resolve theme selections through catalog identities with symlink-safe, bounded, UTF-8-checked source opening.\n71:- [ ] Prepare and atomically commit theme/profile/reload candidates while retaining the last-known-good snapshot on failure.\n72:- [ ] Implement the base, selected pack/mode, owned module contribution, and sparse user override cascade with provenance.\n73:- [ ] Make theme selection durable, fingerprinted, watchable, and revision-consistent across settings/profile changes.\n74:- [ ] Share a restricted CSS parser/lowering and selector matcher between component and theme styles.\n75:- [ ] Share keyframes across theme and component styles and resolve token dependencies, cycles, and inherited custom properties.\n76:- [ ] Make the rendered theme snapshot authoritative for mode, color scheme, contrast, tokens, provenance, and revisioned events.\n77:- [ ] Make theme snapshots immutable and reject duplicate or ambiguous identities for deterministic caching.\n78:- [ ] Add explicit manual, follow-system, and scheduled theme mode policies through the same transaction coordinator.\n84:- [ ] Replace the global translation pool with owner-scoped translators for templates, scripts, manifests, props, debug data, and settings UI.\n85:- [ ] Implement an immutable normalized locale selection with BCP 47 parents, direction, complete fallback chain, and revision.\n86:- [ ] Compile bounded typed message/plural/select entries independently with checked placeholders and shared formatting.\n87:- [ ] Build one immutable catalog snapshot with atomic graph/profile/selection/reload commits and last-known-good recovery.\n88:- [ ] Add targeted ordered language-pack chains, per-module defaults, winning-source provenance, and duplicate precedence checks.\n89:- [ ] Route locale changes through one durable revision-checked settings/profile transaction.\n90:- [ ] Align `mesh.i18n`, `mesh.locale`, runtime/LSP ABI, and read/write capability enforcement.\n91:- [ ] Centralize localized metadata and visible miss handling with owner, fallback, source, and snapshot revision.\n92:- [ ] Open bounded catalogs through contained no-follow source handles and compile them off the shell thread.\n93:- [ ] Drive locale CLI/LSP/extraction/doctor tooling from the canonical graph, and implement or explicitly reject `<i18n>` blocks.\n94:- [ ] Add manual, follow-system, and per-profile locale policies through the same prepare/persist/commit path.\n100:- [ ] Build icon and font resources only from the prepared graph/profile and atomically retain the last-known-good resource snapshot.\n101:- [ ] Preserve declared pack order and reject duplicate canonical IDs, aliases, and ambiguous ownership deterministically.\n102:- [ ] Open module resource assets through contained, no-follow, bounded handles.\n103:- [ ] Implement canonical semantic and dash-generalized icon fallback resolution with required/optional diagnostics.\n104:- [ ] Preserve typed multicolor mappings, source color policy, and mapping provenance.\n105:- [ ] Validate complete packs off the render thread and publish them atomically without partial registry state.\n106:- [ ] Propagate resource revisions/fingerprints through negative lookup, glyph, font, text-layout, and renderer caches.\n107:- [ ] Implement font-pack runtime resolution with logical roles, pack-qualified roles, faces, coverage, and typography tokens.\n108:- [ ] Unify XDG icon/font discovery and lookup into one ordered, refreshable host catalog.\n109:- [ ] Prepare resource parsing and asset handles away from shell/render threads with bounded cancellation.\n110:- [ ] Generate runtime, CLI, LSP, doctor, and debug resource explanations from one effective snapshot.\n111:- [ ] Add a resource coverage advisor for semantic vocabulary and font-script gaps without silently reordering user chains.\n117:- [ ] Make local component imports module-relative, canonicalized, contained, and symlink-safe across compiler, watcher, and LSP paths.\n118:- [ ] Resolve recursive imports by owner scope and canonical target, with collision and cycle diagnostics.\n119:- [ ] Replace lossy block extraction with a span-preserving top-level parser that validates required, unique, attributed blocks and `<i18n>` policy.\n120:- [ ] Parse interpolations and control-flow braces with a real lexer/parser that rejects malformed expressions and preserves spans.\n121:- [ ] Add semantic validation linking `<props>`, `prop()` references, child props, visibility, types, and CSS domains.\n122:- [ ] Select the highest valid value across prop/configuration layers while retaining invalid overrides only in diagnostics.\n123:- [ ] Make JSON-to-prop conversion scalar-only until an explicit structured prop type exists.\n124:- [ ] Normalize and validate `PropDef` constraints, units, options, tokens, and CSS-domain values once.\n125:- [ ] Replace line-oriented script/import/symbol scans with one Luau lexer/parser and source metadata.\n126:- [ ] Carry reliable source spans through component AST nodes, compiler errors, CLI diagnostics, and LSP output.\n132:- [ ] Normalize roles, names, descriptions, hidden state, ARIA aliases, focus, relationships, and visibility after child construction and publish the semantic snapshot.\n133:- [ ] Use visible descendant text in accessible-name precedence and preserve hidden-child and locale behavior.\n134:- [ ] Generate one typed pseudo-state table for indexing, mutation, matching, invalidation, diagnostics, and tests.\n135:- [ ] Make compiler inheritance matching consume the actual element state.\n136:- [ ] Make retained layout transactional, preserve last-known-good geometry, and retry after failure.\n137:- [ ] Use one stateful input dispatcher with pointer capture, press-origin identity, activation semantics, focus eligibility, and invalidation output.\n138:- [ ] Generate element types, source/runtime tags, contracts, events, attributes, style hooks, and accessibility defaults from one schema.\n139:- [ ] Detect CSS custom-property cycles with structured diagnostics and specified invalid-value fallback.\n140:- [ ] Preserve explicit/inherited property masks through retained style resolution and targeted restyle.\n141:- [ ] Derive accessibility focus from canonical live focus state during snapshot generation.\n142:- [ ] Include all shaping inputs and resource/measurer revisions in text measurement contexts and cache keys.\n143:- [ ] Make popover placement tokens and trigger/surface relationships typed, validated, and observable across promotion.\n144:- [ ] Introduce an immutable frame snapshot with phase stamps, semantic diffs, stable identities, and property-based invariant tests.\n150:- [ ] Share visibility, transformed geometry, disabled/inert eligibility, and target filtering across interaction, rendering, focus, scrolling, tooltips, and accessibility.\n151:- [ ] Use one affine transform/clip contract for hit testing, paint bounds, scrolling, and focus geometry.\n152:- [ ] Prevent disabled and inert nodes, including descendants and captured targets, from receiving activation.\n153:- [ ] Preserve keyframe progress across pause/resume and iteration-boundary changes.\n154:- [ ] Add a `MotionPolicy` snapshot for reduced motion across transitions, keyframes, scrolling, inertia, tooltips, and surfaces.\n155:- [ ] Consolidate focus, pointer capture, press origin, gesture ownership, and scroll ownership into one transaction.\n156:- [ ] Preserve the previous discrete value during visibility transitions until the transition completes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
