ocs/spec/01-module-system.md-121-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-122-**Status: target.**\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-123-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-124-Core `mesh` fields (`kind`, `entry`, `uses`, `implements`, `surface`,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:125:`accessibility`, `keybinds`, `i18n`, `theme`, pack sections) are a **closed\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-126-schema**: unknown core fields and near-miss typos produce diagnostics.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-127-`mesh.provides.*` and `mesh.uses.resources.*` are **open namespaces**: unknown\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-128-contribution kinds are preserved in the installed graph as typed opaque records\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-129-so third-party tools/modules can define new contribution kinds without a core\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-130-release. Superseded manifest sections in code (`ServiceSection`,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-131-`DependenciesSection`, `AssetsSection`, `ExportsSection`, `IconsSection`, dead\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-132-generations in `model.rs`) are deleted outright.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-133-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-134-### 3.2 Module kinds\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-135-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-136-| Kind | Purpose | Kind-scoped sections |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-137-| ---- | ------- | -------------------- |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:138:| `frontend` | `.mesh` UI surfaces/widgets for a shell feature | `mesh.surface` (placement), `mesh.accessibility`, `mesh.keybinds`, `mesh.theme` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-139-| `backend` | Provider implementing interfaces (Luau `main.luau`) | `mesh.implements`, `mesh.uses.binaries`, in-script `props {}` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-140-| `interface` | Data-only contract package | `mesh.interface` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-141-| `component` | Embeddable `.mesh` component; **no** `mesh.surface`; consumed via `require(\"@scope/name\")` | — |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-142-| `composition` | An installable shell composition: roots, provider bindings, resources, extension point arrangement | `mesh.compose`, `mesh.extends` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-143-| `library` | Importable Luau helpers; grants no capabilities | `mesh.provides.libraries` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-144-| `theme` | Theme tokens + component defaults (CSS) | `mesh.provides.themes` — see [04](04-styling.md) |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-145-| `icon-pack` | Semantic icon name → asset mappings | `mesh.icon_pack` — see [05](05-icons.md) |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-146-| `font-pack` | Font role → installed family mappings | `mesh.font_pack` — see [06](06-fonts.md) |\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-153-`mesh.surface` carries **placement only** — the compositor concerns CSS cannot\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-154-express. Declare only deltas; omitted fields fall back to core defaults.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-155-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-156-`role` picks which compositor protocol realizes the surface, and thereby which\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-157-of the other fields apply:\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-158-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-159-| `role` | Protocol | Placement fields |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-160-| ------ | -------- | ---------------- |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:161:| `layer` (default) | `zwlr_layer_shell_v1` — shell chrome: panels, launchers, overlays | `anchor`, `layer`, `exclusive_zone`, `keyboard_mode`, `margins` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-162-| `window` | `xdg_toplevel` — an ordinary application window that tiles, floats, moves between workspaces, and closes | `title`, `appId`, `resizable`, `decorations` |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-163-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-164-`visible_on_start` and `blur` apply to both.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-165-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-166-```json\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-167-\"surface\": {\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-168-  \"role\": \"window\",\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-169-  \"title\": { \"t\": \"settings.title\", \"fallback\": \"Settings\" },\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-170-  \"appId\": \"mesh.settings\",\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-171-  \"visible_on_start\": false\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-172-}\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-173-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-174-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-175-Fields belonging to the *other* role are a **graph diagnostic**\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:176:(`surface_role_field_mismatch`), not a silently ignored key: a block that names\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-177-both an anchor and `role: \"window\"` states two incompatible intents, and a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-178-compositor places a toplevel regardless of what the manifest asks.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-179-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-180-The user can move a surface between roles through the sparse settings store\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-181-(`\"surface\": { \"role\": \"window\" }`, [08](08-settings.md)) — the author's `role`\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-182-is a default like every other placement field.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-183-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-184-#### Promotable surfaces\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-187-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-188-`\"promotable\": true` says the surface may be moved between roles *while it is\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-189-running* — popped out of the shell into a window, and docked back. `role` then\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-190-names the role it **starts** as.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-191-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-192-```json\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-193-\"surface\": {\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-194-  \"role\": \"layer\", \"promotable\": true,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:195:  \"anchor\": \"right\", \"layer\": \"overlay\", \"keyboard_mode\": \"on_demand\",\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-196-  \"title\": { \"t\": \"settings.title\", \"fallback\": \"Settings\" },\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-197-  \"appId\": \"mesh.settings\"\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-198-}\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-199-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-200-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-201-A promotable surface is the **one exemption** from the role-mismatch diagnostic\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-202-above: it is realized under both protocols at different points in its life, so\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-203-both field sets apply to it and declaring both is the only way to describe it.\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-212-component's Lua VM, retained tree, page selection, scroll offsets, focus, and\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-213-service subscriptions all survive, because none of them is role-dependent. Three\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-214-paths trigger it:\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-215-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-216-| Trigger | Reaches |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-217-| ------- | ------- |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-218-| `mesh.events.publish(\"shell.set-surface-role\", { surface_id, role })` | in-surface controls (a \"pop out\" button) |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-219-| `shell.toggle-surface-role` on the same channel | a control that flips whichever role is current |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:220:| `shell:promote_surface:<id>`, `shell:demote_surface:<id>`, `shell:toggle_surface_role:<id>` over the automation IPC | a *compositor* keybind, since MESH keybinds are focused-surface actions and cannot grab a global hotkey ([11](11-automation-ipc.md)) |\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-221-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-222-A component tells the two apart in CSS with `:windowed`\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-223-([04 §6.1](04-styling.md)) rather than in script state, so its chrome follows\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-224-the surface's actual role even when the role was changed from outside it. That\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-225-is how one header offers \"pop out\" as a layer surface and \"dock back\" as a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-226-window.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-227-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-228-Because the roles size in opposite directions (below), a promotable surface goes\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-229-through a fresh first-configure pass on every change rather than carrying over a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-230-size measured under the other role.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-231-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-232-#### Promoted embedded widgets\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-233-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-234-**Status: shipped.** An embedded widget can be promoted without promoting its\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-235-parent surface. The shell keeps the widget's retained node and shared surface\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:236:VM in place, removes its pixels from the parent layout, and paints the keyed\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-237-subtree into an independent `xdg_toplevel`. Its state, live `bind:this`\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-238-references, handlers, and service subscriptions therefore continue across the\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-239-move. A widget can be controlled from Luau with\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-240-`shell.promote-widget` / `shell.demote-widget`, each carrying the owning\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:241:`surface_id` and retained `node_key`; `shell.set-widget-role` is the explicit\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-242-role form. Closing the promoted window demotes the widget back into its parent.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-243-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-244-Surface **sizing is CSS**: the laid-out box of the component root\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-245-(`width: 100%` spans the anchored edge, `fit-content` shrinks to content,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-246-`min-*`/`max-*` clamp), measured by `measure_content_size()`. The show/hide\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-247-transition is a CSS `transition` on the root. There are no manifest sizing\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-248-fields and no compatibility aliases. See [03 — Components](03-components.md).\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-249-\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-264-  `:activated`, and `:tiled` pseudo-states on every node of the surface\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-265-  ([04 §6.1](04-styling.md)), so a floating size on the base rule and\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-266-  `width: 100%` on the filling states is the whole mechanism. Note that\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-267-  `\"resizable\": false` and a fullscreen-aware root are contradictory intents —\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-268-  pinning min to max is what stops a compositor from resizing the window at\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-269-  all.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-270-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-271-A window has no say in its position: xdg-shell gives the client none. Placement\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:272:control comes from compositor window rules keyed on `appId`, which defaults to\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-273-the module id.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-274-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-275-Closing a window (title-bar button or compositor binding) **hides** the\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-276-surface; the module, its services, and its Lua state survive, so reopening it is\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-277-the same cheap show as reopening a hidden panel.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-278-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-279-### 3.4 What the manifest no longer carries\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-280-\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-289-- **No surface sizing / `display_transition` / `size_policy`.** *(Shipped —\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-290-  removed.)*\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-291-- **No inline icon mappings in frontends.** Mappings live in icon-pack\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-292-  modules; frontends keep only `iconRequirements` and pack deps. *(Shipped\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-293-  direction; redundant sections are deletion targets.)*\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-294-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-295-## 4. Interfaces\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-296-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:297:**Status: shipped** for the registry, inline and external JSON contracts, keyed\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-298-external declarations, type/event validation, runtime proxy typing, LSP\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-299-contract completions, and relationship metadata. Substantial interface modules\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-300-may move the same JSON contract object to a separate `contract.json` referenced\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-301-by `module.json`; tiny contracts may remain inline. This reduces manifest noise\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-302-without adding another language or execution model. **Target:** generated\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-303-provider stubs, mocks, standalone documentation, and compatibility reports.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-304-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-305-An interface is a named, versioned declaration of:\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-382-      \"name\": \"mesh.audio\",\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-383-      \"version\": \"1.0\",\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-384-      \"contract\": \"contract.json\"\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-385-    }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-386-  }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-387-}\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-388-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-389-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:390:`contract.json` uses keyed `state`, `methods`, `events`, and `types` objects.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-391-It declares descriptions, units, ranges, errors, capabilities, and optional\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-392-feature groups. Tooling compiles inline and external forms into the same\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-393-canonical `InterfaceContract` representation. Runtime validation and LSP\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-394-completion use its strict Luau field, argument, return, and event-payload types.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-395-Provider stubs, mocks, standalone documentation, and compatibility reports\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-396-remain target tooling.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-397-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-398-- **Type grammar.** Every `type`/`returns` expression is validated at graph\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-474-      }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-475-    }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-476-  }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-477-}\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-478-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-479-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-480-A **host** declares which points it renders and lays them out. Hosting is\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-481-explicit and versioned because a host renders another module's UI inside its own\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:482:surface — a trust decision, never an inference:\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-483-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-484-```json\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-485-\"hosts\": { \"mesh.settings.page\": { \"version\": \">=1.0\", \"layout\": \"column\" } }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-486-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-487-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-488-```html\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-489-<slot extension-point=\"mesh.settings.page\" />\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-490-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-491-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-492-Hosts may also expose a contract as named customizable slots. These slots use\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-493-explicit composition/profile placement instead of automatically rendering every\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:494:contribution. The host record contains a slots map whose keys are stable local\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-495-names and whose defaults are stable source-module-id:contribution-id\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-496-references. Markup addresses the same record with a static name,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-497-extension-point, and customizable mode.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-498-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-499-A customizable slot name is unique in its component entry and must have a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-500-matching host record. Existing slots remain automatic unless explicitly marked\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-501-customizable.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-502-\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-527-- Render order is `(order, source module id, contribution id)` — deterministic\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-528-  across rebuilds.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-529-- `multiple: false` means at most one contribution; more is\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-530-  `extension_point_overfilled`.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-531-- Contribution props are typechecked against the declaration using the same\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-532-  type grammar as service contracts (§4).\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-533-- **A contribution creates no dependency edge on the host.** The edge terminates\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-534-  at the contract, so a host that itself depends on a contributor is not a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:535:  cycle. Module-keyed slots made that adapter pattern unloadable.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-536-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-537-Diagnostics: `unknown_extension_point`, `extension_point_version_mismatch`,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-538-`invalid_extension_point_props`, `extension_point_overfilled`, and the\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-539-informational `unhosted_contribution` (a valid state when the host is installed\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-540-but not composed).\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-541-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-542-### 4.4 Events — one communication primitive\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-543-\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-610-  **settings store** ([08](08-settings.md)), not the root graph. The root\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-611-  graph owns module-graph decisions; settings own look-and-feel values.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-612-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-613-### 5.1 Multiple instances of a frontend module\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-614-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-615-**Status: target.**\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-616-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-617-Module identity is not the only surface identity. The root graph may declare\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:618:named instances with the `module-id#instance-id` key form:\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-619-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-620-```json\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-621-\"layout\": {\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-622-  \"entrypoint\": \"@mesh/navigation-bar:main\",\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-623-  \"instances\": {\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-624-    \"@mesh/navigation-bar#top\":    { \"surface\": { \"anchor\": \"top\" } },\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-625-    \"@mesh/navigation-bar#bottom\": { \"surface\": { \"anchor\": \"bottom\" } }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-626-  }\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-627-}\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-628-```\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-629-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-630-A bare module reference means the implicit `#default` instance. The instance\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:631:key scopes surface bookkeeping, the settings namespace (per-instance props,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-632-[08 §3](08-settings.md)), and `self.storage`. No new mechanism — the existing\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:633:per-instance scoping keys on.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-634-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-635-### 5.2 Composition modules\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-636-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-637-**Status: shipped.**\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-638-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-639-A profile alone is a config file: no version, no dependencies, no lock entry,\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-640-no capability review. A **composition module** is a profile that is also a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-641-module, so a whole shell family can be installed, published, pinned, updated,\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-715-→ derived composition → profile, most specific winning per field, with two\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-716-deliberate exceptions:\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-717-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-718-- **Ordered resource chains replace rather than merge.** An icon or font chain\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-719-  is an ordered fallback list; interleaving two orderings has no meaning.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-720-- **A user may deactivate an inherited root but not delete it.** Deletion is not\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-721-  expressible in a delta layer, and an update would resurrect it anyway.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-722-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md:723:A user override keyed to a root the composition no longer declares is\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-724-**retained and reported** (`orphaned_profile_override`), never dropped —\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-725-discarding it would lose the user's work on every upstream rename.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-726-`mesh profile prune` clears them on request.\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-727-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-728-Profiles are stored as `profiles/<id>.json`; `active-profile` contains the\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-729-selected id. Their positive root list is not an installed-module allow-list:\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-730-only user-composed roots and explicit choices are stored, while declared module\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-731-dependencies, resource dependencies, interface modules, and a sole compatible\n--\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-754-\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-755-Presence composes an instance; `active: false` temporarily removes it while\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-756-preserving identity and overrides. `surface` on an instance is sparse: omitted\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-757-fields inherit `mesh.surface`, and only user changes are written. Installing a\ndocs/spec/01-module-system.md-758-frontend directly