{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/BACKLOG.md | sed -n '300,380p' && nl -ba docs/BACKLOG.md | sed -n '520,625p'\"","aggregated_output":"   300\t- [ ] Replace heuristic Luau/JSON scanners with standards-compliant parsers and source-span data.\n   301\t- [ ] Support workspace-folder-only initialization and versioned `didChange` refresh generations.\n   302\t- [ ] Select manifest flavors from parsed structure, not textual substring checks.\n   303\t- [ ] Make hover consume the current registry and expose service field/command documentation.\n   304\t- [ ] Restrict definition resolution to existing module-contained imports.\n   305\t- [ ] Preserve Unicode JSON escapes, registry generations, and secure import provenance in authoring diagnostics.\n   306\t\n   307\t## Foundation contracts\n   308\t\n   309\t## Module system\n   310\t\n   311\tThe 2026-06-18 redesign largely shipped: canonical `module.json` with\n   312\t`mesh.uses` / `mesh.provides` / `mesh.implements`, the graph as single source of\n   313\ttruth, typed graph diagnostics, library modules, and resource packs. Remaining:\n   314\t\n   315\t- [ ] Close module filesystem escapes before any package mutation or source\n   316\t      read: validate canonical module IDs, contain all entry/import/asset paths,\n   317\t      reject Git symlinks, and remove CLI uninstall traversal. [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/02-module-system-and-installation/improvements.md).\n   318\t- [ ] Make installed-graph activation fail closed and build catalogs/provider\n   319\t      registries only from its enabled, compatible candidate set; preserve the\n   320\t      last known-good runtime when graph validation fails. [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/02-module-system-and-installation/improvements.md).\n   321\t- [ ] Replace the duplicate CLI/shell package implementations with one locked,\n   322\t      journaled transaction engine covering source, root, lock, profiles, and\n   323\t      runtime preparation/commit/rollback. [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/02-module-system-and-installation/improvements.md).\n   324\t- [ ] Enforce required/optional module dependencies, module/interface version\n   325\t      ranges, composition pins/closure, and duplicate contract/contribution IDs\n   326\t      before activation rather than leaving conflicts diagnostic-only.\n   327\t- [ ] Make the canonical `module.json` loader the only production path; legacy\n   328\t      manifests remain migration diagnostics, never runnable compatibility\n   329\t      inputs.\n   330\t- [ ] Make module lifecycle and health authoritative across graph, frontend, and\n   331\t      backend states, including explicit unload/recovery/quarantine and service\n   332\t      unavailability delivery.\n   333\t- [ ] Align the lock schema with the specification and populate dependency and\n   334\t      composition provenance so uninstall/update/rollback decisions operate on\n   335\t      complete state.\n   336\t- [ ] Move the remaining built-in debug and theme/locale service behavior\n   337\t      behind generic providers. Startup sounds and backend profiling use the\n   338\t      generic contract/runtime path; core-owned service state still branches.\n   339\t      _(detail: \"Module system — remaining open follow-ups\")_\n   340\t- [ ] **Deferred — unify the four contribution schemas.** Theme, icons, i18n,\n   341\t      and keybinds under one `contributes` shape, only where they share honest\n   342\t      structure. Revisit after profiles land. Capability inference and a\n   343\t      parallel inline-interface path were both rejected: they trade conceptual\n   344\t      simplicity for typing simplicity, which is the failure mode that redesign\n   345\t      set out to avoid.\n   346\t\n   347\t## Service contracts\n   348\t\n   349\t- [ ] Remove shared `__mesh_svc_*` Luau state: keep service payloads in a\n   350\t      capability-filtered per-context/Rust-owned store so one module cannot read\n   351\t      or mutate another module's service state. [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/03-service-contracts/improvements.md).\n   352\t- [ ] Replace the additive interface registry with one immutable, atomic\n   353\t      graph-derived service catalog binding each consumer to the active compatible\n   354\t      contract/provider/version/policy generation. [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/03-service-contracts/improvements.md).\n   355\t- [ ] Compile and enforce complete contracts end to end: canonical unique names,\n   356\t      recursive named/array types, consistent optional semantics, typed method\n   357\t      inputs/results, last-known-good state, and event payloads.\n   358\t- [ ] Make service methods correlated request/response transactions with typed\n   359\t      invocation failures, deadlines/cancellation, explicit coalescing outcomes,\n   360\t      and rollback/settlement for optimistic `stateBinding` writes.\n   361\t- [ ] Gate provider/profile commits on validated readiness and buffered initial\n   362\t      state; immediately deliver unavailability and reject all state/events/results\n   363\t      from stopped or obsolete provider generations.\n   364\t- [ ] Diff the complete compiled contract in consumer and provider directions,\n   365\t      load external candidate contracts, align LSP/static analysis/codegen with\n   366\t      the runtime ABI, and remove the unused transitional `ServiceRegistry`.\n   367\t\n   368\t## Themes\n   369\t\n   370\t- [ ] Make graph-authorized theme descriptors the only catalog/loader, with\n   371\t      contained mode sources and one composed base/pack/module/user cascade;\n   372\t      remove the private `config/themes` manifest and legacy JSON paths. [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/04-themes/improvements.md).\n   373\t- [ ] Make theme selection, profile switching, graph changes, and hot reload one\n   374\t      durable prepare/commit transaction that preserves the last-known-good\n   375\t      snapshot, refreshes watches/catalog state, and never exits on bad CSS.\n   376\t- [ ] Share the restricted CSS/token/keyframe lowering path between themes and\n   377\t      components so pseudo-states, inherited custom properties, token recipes,\n   378\t      and general theme keyframes work or produce source-located diagnostics.\n   379\t- [ ] Complete `mesh.theme` and settings with modes, sparse token overrides,\n   380\t      provenance, explicit color-scheme/contrast, and revisioned authoritative\n   520\tpromotion\")_\n   521\t\n   522\t## Performance\n   523\t\n   524\tFull history, baselines, and the **rejected-experiments table** are in\n   525\t[`.planning/log/performance-log.md`](../.planning/log/performance-log.md).\n   526\tCheck it before starting: several of the obvious approaches below have already\n   527\tbeen measured and reverted.\n   528\t\n   529\tEvery optimization lands with a representative benchmark, and a checked relative\n   530\tgate where the win is structural.\n   531\t\n   532\t### Render pipeline\n   533\t\n   534\t- [ ] **The narrow service path never engages for real modules.** It requires a\n   535\t      template to interpolate the service field directly, but every shipped\n   536\t      component reads services in Luau and binds derived variables — so\n   537\t      `narrow_nodes` is empty, invalidation falls back to `TREE_REBUILD`, and\n   538\t      every poll is a full rebuild plus 100%-of-surface damage. Measured on the\n   539\t      navigation bar 2026-08-08: 240/240 frames full-surface, ~4 such frames per\n   540\t      second at rest. Needs script-level service reads to feed\n   541\t      `service_field_reads`, or a different narrowing signal.\n   542\t- [ ] A root-level `backdrop-filter` collapses all partial damage to the whole\n   543\t      surface (`expand_damage_for_blur_regions` unions with the full blurred\n   544\t      region), and `.nav-shell` carries one. Latent today because damage is\n   545\t      already full-surface for the reason above; it becomes the next ceiling as\n   546\t      soon as that is fixed.\n   547\t- [ ] Continue widening generation shortcuts to per-node dirty scoping and\n   548\t      unify changed-node fingerprints across the retained, render, and display\n   549\t      layers; geometry-only retained snapshots are split out now.\n   550\t- [ ] Display-list segment/rope command storage → v1.21. Command arrays are\n   551\t      still flattened per ancestor. Replay must consume segments directly\n   552\t      instead of eagerly re-flattening them — an eager reconstruction was tried\n   553\t      and reverted (see log).\n   554\t- [ ] Close the Section 12 correctness gaps before further paint optimization:\n   555\t      unify paint fingerprints and topology generations, implement complete\n   556\t      transforms/effect compositing/border lowering, and revision text/icon\n   557\t      caches. [Section 12 audit](../.planning/log/sections/12-rendering-and-paint/improvements.md)\n   558\t\n   559\t### Style\n   560\t\n   561\t- [ ] Typed style declarations end-to-end: resolve theme tokens to typed values\n   562\t      once per theme load; `apply_declaration` consumes typed values, strings\n   563\t      only for diagnostics (E). Static literals now pre-lower; typed property\n   564\t      values and one-time token lowering remain. _(detail: \"P2 — typing &\n   565\t      interning\")_\n   566\t- [ ] Interaction frames still re-apply string style declarations per node —\n   567\t      folds into typed declarations and narrower invalidation.\n   568\t      _(detail: \"P2 — architecture\")_\n   569\t- [ ] A tree-rebuild frame restyles memo-reused subtrees too. Component memo\n   570\t      entries are stored pre-restyle (position-independent by design), so a\n   571\t      reused page pays a full style walk and copy-on-write anyway — 2.8ms of an\n   572\t      8.6ms Appearance service frame. Needs styled memo entries, or a\n   573\t      \"styles still valid\" mark the restyle walk can skip.\n   574\t\n   575\t### Typing and interning\n   576\t\n   577\t- [ ] Interned `Symbol` / `TagId` types and a typed `WidgetNode`. Attributes,\n   578\t      module ids, and element tags are done; widget-tree **tags**, attribute\n   579\t      **values**, and the broader symbol types remain. Profiling now puts the\n   580\t      dominant remaining build cost in style resolution, not further attribute\n   581\t      work. _(detail: \"P2 — typing & interning\")_\n   582\t\n   583\t### Composition\n   584\t\n   585\t### Threading\n   586\t\n   587\t- [ ] Parallelize paint across surfaces: phase-split `render_components` into a\n   588\t      serial VM-bound phase and a parallel paint/SHM phase (rayon) (K).\n   589\t- [ ] Pipeline paint of frame N against script work of frame N+1, after the\n   590\t      per-surface split.\n   591\t- [ ] Tile-parallel raster for large damage, above a measured threshold only.\n   592\t- [ ] Move blocking file IO off the shell thread — i18n catalog mounts,\n   593\t      settings and theme reloads, and icon/SVG cache-miss rasterization on the\n   594\t      paint path — via `spawn_blocking` plus completion events.\n   595\t\n   596\t### Runtime boundary\n   597\t\n   598\t- [ ] Apply one authoritative sandbox/resource policy to every Luau realm:\n   599\t      enforce instruction, memory, output, queue, storage, and child-process\n   600\t      budgets, with timeout cleanup and quarantine. [Section 11 audit](../.planning/log/sections/11-luau-runtime-and-sandbox/improvements.md).\n   601\t- [ ] Replace backend task aborts and early-return cleanup with an idempotent\n   602\t      lifecycle supervisor that stages provider generations, flushes storage,\n   603\t      reaps streams, and publishes one truthful terminal result. [Section 11 audit](../.planning/log/sections/11-luau-runtime-and-sandbox/improvements.md).\n   604\t- [ ] Move `mesh.exec` and stream handling behind bounded cancellable workers\n   605\t      with stable stream IDs, exit/reap events, output limits, and executable\n   606\t      path/argument policy. [Section 11 audit](../.planning/log/sections/11-luau-runtime-and-sandbox/improvements.md).\n   607\t- [ ] Make backend commands and events typed, correlated, generation-aware,\n   608\t      transactional, and bounded; define explicit coalescing keys and terminal\n   609\t      overflow/timeout results. [Section 11 audit](../.planning/log/sections/11-luau-runtime-and-sandbox/improvements.md).\n   610\t- [ ] Move default runtime storage to secure durable XDG state with user-only\n   611\t      permissions, quotas, recovery, and single-writer/revision semantics.\n   612\t      [Section 11 audit](../.planning/log/sections/11-luau-runtime-and-sandbox/improvements.md).\n   613\t- [ ] Make reload transactional and backend callback handles generation-stable:\n   614\t      replace stale Lua environments, preserve one backend `self`, and prevent\n   615\t      pre-ready or old-generation updates from reaching consumers. [Section 11 audit](../.planning/log/sections/11-luau-runtime-and-sandbox/improvements.md).\n   616\t\n   617\t- [ ] Push-based backend host API primitives (D-Bus signal subscribe, fd/socket\n   618\t      watch, stream adoption) so providers are event-driven and polling is the\n   619\t      fallback (C). **Measured 2026-08-08:** the shipped polls fork ~3 processes\n   620\t      per second (`hyprctl` 500ms, `wpctl` 1000ms, `brightnessctl` 2000ms) and\n   621\t      cost 6.4% of a core continuously — 32x the whole shell render loop at rest\n   622\t      (0.2%) — mostly in dynamic-linker startup, for no state change. Includes evaluating `pw-dump --monitor` as a real volume\n   623\t      event source; `pw-mon` emits no `changed:` block for volume.\n   624\t- [ ] Handler sync still reads compound table globals, because nested in-place\n   625\t      mutations never assign through `_ENV`. Eliminating those reads needs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
