e revisions still match.\n168:- [ ] Enforce one sandbox/resource policy for every Luau realm, including instruction, memory, output, queue, storage, and child-process budgets.\n169:- [ ] Keep service state Rust-owned, generation-aware, and capability-filtered instead of exposing shared globals.\n170:- [ ] Route every backend early return, callback failure, stop, and crash through idempotent cleanup and one terminal lifecycle record.\n171:- [ ] Make unsubscribe-safe event iteration and independent subscriber failure reporting explicit.\n172:- [ ] Give stream subprocesses stable identities, bounded queues, exit events, awaited reaping, and shutdown semantics.\n173:- [ ] Move `mesh.exec` off the async backend loop and enforce cancellation, deadlines, executable policy, and output limits.\n174:- [ ] Replace basename executable grants with canonical path/argument capability policy.\n175:- [ ] Move default runtime storage to secure durable XDG state with permissions, quotas, atomic recovery, and revisioned writers.\n176:- [ ] Make backend command dispatch typed, correlated, transactional, coalescable, generation-aware, and bounded.\n177:- [ ] Gate event and side-effect queues through one typed authorization/resource boundary before acceptance.\n178:- [ ] Represent locale as a host-owned per-context cell updated with the translation snapshot.\n179:- [ ] Treat Luau `nil` writes as explicit deletions in Rust state and dependency invalidation.\n180:- [ ] Restrict provider event publication to provider-owned handles and isolate subscriber callback failures.\n181:- [ ] Preserve one stable backend `self` and event/storage handles for each runtime generation.\n182:- [ ] Publish validated initial provider state before atomically marking the provider ready.\n183:- [ ] Compile and swap a fresh Luau environment on reload, preserving only explicit durable storage.\n184:- [ ] Stage backend top-level execution so host side effects cannot escape a failed `start(self)`.\n185:- [ ] Bound command/event ingress, JSON depth/bytes, event counts, and aggregate runtime resource budgets.\n186:- [ ] Separate effective read and control grants and enforce them through both proxy and shell paths.\n187:- [ ] Reconcile changed poll intervals after every stream callback.\n188:- [ ] Return recoverable host-installation errors instead of panicking during backend setup.\n189:- [ ] Introduce a per-module `RuntimeSession` combining realm, host, resource broker, lifecycle, state, supervisor, health, backoff, and quarantine.\n195:- [ ] Make `PixelCanvasSession` storage-safe so mapped drawing surfaces cannot outlive backing allocations.\n196:- [ ] Lower asymmetric four-edge borders and four-corner radii correctly.\n197:- [ ] Use one cumulative affine transform/clip model across paint, damage, blur, descendants, and interaction.\n198:- [ ] Lower node opacity and blend mode as isolated compositing groups instead of per primitive.\n199:- [ ] Include paint-order/topology changes in display-list generations and stable equal-z ordering.\n200:- [ ] Unify dirty contracts and paint signatures for all content/style fields, including controls, text, icons, and variables.\n201:- [ ] Include font/resource revisions in text style painting and all glyph/font/text cache keys.\n202:- [ ] Make backdrop blur an explicit renderer/backend capability with validated fallback behavior.\n203:- [ ] Use one fractional-scale rounding policy across layout, buffer, paint, copy, and protocol damage.\n204:- [ ] Preserve release batch/barrier metrics in diagnostics and debug telemetry.\n205:- [ ] Validate caller lineage before trusting generation shortcuts.\n206:- [ ] Include resource revisions in retained-present decisions and cache invalidation.\n207:- [ ] Preserve pending damage and avoid acknowledging unshown frames after presentation errors.\n208:- [ ] Move resource decode and rasterization off the frame thread through a bounded resource broker.\n209:- [ ] Enforce byte- and dimension-based cache budgets for decoded assets, fonts, glyphs, text, Skia, PixelBuffer, and SHM allocations.\n210:- [ ] Introduce a typed frame paint plan with immutable inputs, topology, transforms, effect regions, replay spans, and exact logical/device damage.\n216:- [ ] Enforce the author-only `promotable` guard for settings, IPC, and live role changes.\n217:- [ ] Remove or formally protect `promotable` from user-overridable/ejected settings.\n218:- [ ] Validate manifest surface enums and role constraints with canonical parsers before graph resolution.\n219:- [ ] Include blur and window decorations in semantic presentation change detection.\n220:- [ ] Route settings-driven role reloads through the same transactional transition supervisor as explicit promotion.\n221:- [ ] Share role-field metadata across manifest diagnostics, settings validation, ejection, and protocol lowering.\n222:- [ ] Preserve localization identity and distinguish effective values from overrides during configuration ejection.\n223:- [ ] Use typed unmeasured/content/surface/wire extents at the shell/presentation boundary.\n224:- [ ] Replace split surface field lists with a revisioned semantic policy diff and generation.\n225:- [ ] Build the policy compiler producing declared contracts, effective snapshots, and typed transition plans.\n231:- [ ] Return typed create/configure/present/lost outcomes, cache only accepted generations, and retain damage for missing surfaces.\n232:- [ ] Route close, dismiss, parent destruction, role replacement, and connection loss through one idempotent teardown supervisor.\n233:- [ ] Replace incomplete presentation hashes and warm region caches with typed semantic diffs and object/configure/frame generations.\n234:- [ ] Preserve click-grab seat and serial identity through input normalization, popup requests, and one-shot configuration.\n235:- [ ] Gate popup reposition by negotiated protocol version and validate popup role, parent, identity, and reparenting.\n236:- [ ] Use one authoritative logical extent for paint, buffer validation, viewport, regions, attach, and queries.\n237:- [ ] Commit opaque, blur, and other surface-state changes even when pixel damage is empty.\n238:- [ ] Separate frame-callback waiting from buffer-release backpressure and prevent hot retry loops.\n239:- [ ] Make input ownership per seat and cancel pointer, touch, gesture, focus, and repeat transactions during teardown.\n240:- [ ] Validate buffer length/stride/scale, propagate attach/region errors, expose connection loss, and reap clipboard children.\n241:- [ ] Replace the recorder backend with a deterministic protocol-state lifecycle simulator plus a focused live compositor matrix.\n242:- [ ] Add full pointer-button identity and IME/text-input-v3 support while preserving normalized Escape behavior.\n243:- [ ] Build the transactional, capability-aware presentation engine with version reporting, reactive popups, multi-output membership, per-seat input, and shared SHM/dmabuf/GPU frame contracts.\n249:- [ ] Replace split profile/runtime mutation with one immutable activation plan and atomic runtime-generation commit.\n250:- [ ] Reconcile backend enable/disable and every graph delta through the same activation coordinator.\n251:- [ ] Tag backend tasks, bridges, messages, events, results, and restart deadlines with activation generations and provider epochs.\n252:- [ ] Make frontend/backend stop, unmount, storage flush, worker join, and shutdown cleanup explicit and idempotent.\n253:- [ ] Give detached workers owned wake handles and lifecycle guards that outlive the eventfd until join.\n254:- [ ] Isolate component/runtime callback, tick, build, render, and reload failures with placeholders, diagnostics, and quarantine.\n255:- [ ] Replace static startup watching with a managed generation-aware watch set and bounded polling fallback.\n256:- [ ] Process CoreRequest effects through one fair bounded scheduler with causal budgets and cycle detection.\n257:- [ ] Publish provider unavailable/recovery transitions from committed provider generations.\n258:- [ ] Route control-plane writes through declared durable revisions and ordered settings/theme/locale effect batches.\n259:- [ ] Distinguish intentional legacy/no-profile operation from invalid configured graph/profile recovery.\n260:- [ ] Connect package journal commit/rollback to runtime activation so disk and live state share one recoverable transaction.\n261:- [ ] Introduce `ActiveSnapshot` with candidate preview in hidden surfaces and an explicit quiescing-to-stopped shutdown state machine.\n267:- [ ] Make uninstall path-safe and reject traversal/symlink escapes before recursive deletion.\n268:- [ ] Make package mutations atomic, journaled, crash-recoverable, and failure-injection tested.\n269:- [ ] Make live profile switching use typed acknowledgements and exact-generation recovery.\n270:- [ ] Make CLI and shell use one package ownership and transaction contract.\n271:- [ ] Refresh one canonical graph-authoring snapshot for CLI, doctor, LSP, and runtime consumers.\n272:- [ ] Generate LSP manifest/schema validation from runtime contracts instead of duplicated under-approximations.\n273:- [ ] Convert all LSP positions to UTF-16 code units at the protocol boundary.\n274:- [ ] Make `--replace` and CLI flags enforce their documented typed behavior.\n275:- [ ] Make LSP analysis syntax-aware with recoverable partial ASTs and useful mid-edit diagnostics.\n276:- [ ] Replace heuristic Luau/JSON scanners with standards-compliant parsers and source-span data.\n277:- [ ] Support workspace-folder-only initialization and versioned `didChange` refresh generations.\n278:- [ ] Select manifest flavors from parsed structure, not textual substring checks.\n279:- [ ] Make hover consume the current registry and expose service field/command documentation.\n280:- [ ] Restrict definition resolution to existing module-contained imports.\n281:- [ ] Preserve Unicode JSON escapes, registry generations, and secure import provenance in authoring diagnostics.\n291:- [ ] Close module filesystem escapes before any package mutation or source\n294:- [ ] Make installed-graph activation fail closed and build catalogs/provider\n297:- [ ] Replace the duplicate CLI/shell package implementations with one locked,\n300:- [ ] Enforce required/optional module dependencies, module/interface version\n303:- [ ] Make the canonical `module.json` loader the only production path; legacy\n306:- [ ] Make module lifecycle and health authoritative across graph, frontend, and\n309:- [ ] Align the lock schema with the specification and populate dependency and\n312:- [ ] Move the remaining built-in debug and theme/locale service behavior\n316:- [ ] **Deferred — unify the four contribution schemas.** Theme, icons, i18n,\n325:- [ ] Replace the additive interface registry with one immutable, atomic\n328:- [ ] Compile and enforce complete contracts end to end: canonical unique names,\n331:- [ ] Make service methods correlated request/response transactions with typed\n334:- [ ] Gate provider/profile commits on validated readiness and buffered initial\n337:- [ ] Diff the complete compiled contract in consumer and provider directions,\n343:- [ ] Make graph-authorized theme descriptors the only catalog/loader, with\n346:- [ ] Make theme selection, profile switching, graph changes, and hot reload one\n349:- [ ] Share the restricted CSS/token/keyframe lowering path between themes and\n352:- [ ] Complete `mesh.theme` and settings with modes, sparse token overrides,\n358:- [ ] Replace per-surface locale engines and the cross-module global key pool\n361:- [ ] Make locale selection a durable revisioned settings/profile transaction:\n364:- [ ] Compile bounded typed catalogs with per-entry diagnostics, interpolation,\n367:- [ ] Route templates, Luau, manifests, props, generated settings, and debug data\n370:- [ ] Drive locale CLI/LSP/doctor, extraction, missing-key and provenance tooling\n376:- [ ] Replace discovery-time global resource registration with one immutable,\n379:- [ ] Make icon resolution deterministic and complete: canonical owner-scoped\n382:- [ ] Complete font-pack runtime support with logical and pack-qualified roles,\n385:- [ ] Unify XDG and font discovery into a refreshable host catalog; propagate\n388:- [ ] Remove legacy icon config and discovery authorities, and drive bounded\n394:- [ ] Replace lossy `.mesh` block extraction and ad-hoc template preprocessing\n397:- [ ] Make component compilation resolve imports per owner, enforce module-root\n400:- [ ] Make the `<props>` contract one normalized typed value pipeline: reject\n406:- [ ] Establish unique `NodeId` tree identity and reject duplicate/unknown\n408:- [ ] Generate element contracts, runtime types, attributes, events, and\n410:- [ ] Consolidate interaction, style invalidation, retained layout, and\n413:- [ ] Normalize ARIA/visibility/name semantics after child construction and\n418:- [ ] Unify visibility, transformed geometry, disabled/inert eligibility, and\n421:- [ ] Define a canonical interaction transaction for focus, pointer capture,\n424:- [ ] Complete motion semantics: pause/resume, stable animation identity,\n427:- [ ] Implement or safely gate the public `box-shadow` parser and add the\n432:- [ ] Compile, validate, watch, invalidate, and reload primary and\n435:- [ ] Gate service payload publication on capabilities and replace the\n438:- [ ] Complete frontend runtime lifecycle and recovery: dispatch mount/unmount,\n441:- [ ] Unify template expression semantics and root-scope validation around the\n444:- [ ] Split the renderer/Wayland/package/debug policy out of the\n449:- [ ] Replace split profile/runtime mutation with one revisioned activation\n453:- [ ] Reconcile every live graph delta, including backend module enable/disable;\n456:- [ ] Add explicit frontend unmount and graceful backend stop/join, then route\n459:- [ ] Replace the static startup watcher with a healthy, generation-aware watch\n462:- [ ] Centralize CoreRequest effects in one fair bounded scheduler and isolate\n465:- [ ] Make shell control-plane propagation coherent: publish provider\n471:- [ ] Move CLI install/update/rollback/uninstall/profile mutations behind one\n474:- [ ] Derive and refresh one canonical graph-authoring snapshot for CLI, doctor,\n477:- [ ] Make LSP parsing and protocol boundaries correct and syntax-aware:\n507:- [ ] **The narrow service path never engages for real modules.** It requires a\n515:- [ ] A root-level `backdrop-filter` collapses all partial damage to the whole\n520:- [ ] Continue widening generation shortcuts to per-node dirty scoping and\n523:- [ ] Display-list segment/rope command storage → v1.21. Command arrays are\n527:- [ ] Close the Section 12 correctness gaps before further paint optimization:\n534:- [ ] Typed style declarations end-to-end: resolve theme tokens to typed values\n539:- [ ] Interaction frames still re-apply string style declarations per node —\n542:- [ ] A tree-rebuild frame restyles memo-reused subtrees too. Component memo\n550:- [ ] Interned `Symbol` / `TagId` types and a typed `WidgetNode`. Attributes,\n560:- [ ] Parallelize paint across surfaces: phase-split `render_components` into a\n562:- [ ] Pipeline paint of frame N against script work of frame N+1, after the\n564:- [ ] Tile-parallel raster for large damage, above a measured threshold only.\n565:- [ ] Move blocking file IO off the shell thread — i18n catalog mounts,\n571:- [ ] Apply one authoritative sandbox/resource policy to every Luau realm:\n574:- [ ] Replace backend task aborts and early-return cleanup with an idempotent\n577:- [ ] Move `mesh.exec` and stream handling behind bounded cancellable workers\n580:- [ ] Make backend commands and events typed, correlated, generation-aware,\n583:- [ ] Move default runtime storage to secure durable XDG state with user-only\n586:- [ ] Make reload transactional and backend callback handles generation-stable:\n590:- [ ] Push-based backend host API primitives (D-Bus signal subscribe, fd/socket\n597:- [ ] Handler sync still reads compound table globals, because nested in-place\n601:- [ ] Storage reads still clone per Lua access. Needs shared immutable JSON\n607:- [ ] Validate manifest surface enums and role-specific fields before\n610:- [ ] Protect the author-only `promotable` contract and route settings-driven\n613:- [ ] Unify role-field metadata, settings/ejection semantics, and manifest\n616:- [ ] Replace split surface-config field lists with a revisioned semantic\n619:- [ ] Make unmeasured/content/padded/physical surface extents typed at the\n625:- [ ] Establish one canonical render-frame snapshot and transform/clip model;\n628:- [ ] Make `PixelBuffer` allocation fallible and bounded, and make\n631:- [ ] Complete paint semantics for opacity layers, four-edge borders,\n634:- [ ] Replace path-only font/glyph/text caches and synchronous icon/font decode\n637:- [ ] Make partial-present capability, layer balance, diagnostics, and\n643:- [ ] Make presentation lifecycle transactional and observable: typed\n646:- [ ] Replace presentation fingerprints and warm region caches with typed diffs\n649:- [ ] Make popup promotion capability- and identity-safe: carry click seat/serial,\n652:- [ ] Unify resolved logical/physical surface extents and make SHM buffer-release\n655:- [ ] Replace the recording-only presentation test backend with a deterministic\n658:- [ ] Direct Skia paint into the mapped SHM canvas for full-present frames,\n661:- [ ] Rotation transforms allocate a temp `PixelBuffer` and repaint the subtree\n667:- [ ] Narrow frontend catalog index rebuilds to graph deltas. Compiled sources\n673:- [ ] GPU rendering backend after retained layout, smart invalidation, and\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
