{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' .planning/log/2026-08.md\"","aggregated_output":"# August 2026\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Retain last-known-good theme candidates\n\n`4d11e431` · area: theme/profile/reload transactions\n\nProfile switches prepare graph-selected theme sources before committing the\ncandidate runtime. Reload parsing and component invalidation failures now keep\nthe prior theme/watch snapshot and record `theme_reload_rejected`; successful\nprofile theme changes preserve the existing catalog while replacing only the\nprepared active snapshot.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Open theme selections through contained graph sources\n\n`73dcc5ad` · area: theme source security and selection\n\nTheme selection now accepts only graph-scoped catalog identities. Their mode\nsources open beneath the owning module root with no-follow directory/file\nhandles, bounded reads, regular-file checks, and UTF-8 validation; registration\nand reload use the same boundary. Legacy free-form selection paths are rejected\nby the shell control path.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Build the graph-authorized theme catalog\n\n`447d2b43` · area: theme catalog and module graph\n\nEnabled canonical theme contributions now form one deterministic catalog keyed\nby owner-scoped identity. Descriptors retain owner module, label, ordered modes,\nvalidated default mode, and a module-root-relative source handle. Runtime theme\nregistration consumes that catalog instead of scanning `config/themes`.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Commit signed module provenance verification\n\n`fcd5fd47` · area: module provenance and candidate planning\n\nThe detached `module.sig` verifier, root-graph trust anchors, lock/graph\nprovenance checks, installer/update enforcement, and specification updates are\nnow committed. The implementation fails closed for unknown keys, malformed or\nchanged signatures, unsupported algorithms, and unverifiable verified tiers.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Close the unified service call transaction improvement\n\n`working tree` · area: service call lifecycle and optimistic state\n\nThe existing call path now covers the full improvement: Luau awaitable tickets\npublish one correlated CallId, shell routing preserves it, backend controls\nenforce deadlines and cancellation, coalescing produces explicit superseded\noutcomes, debug/profiling records retain the ID, and optimistic state writes\nsettle or roll back against that same transaction. Terminal delivery is\nidempotent and stale provider generations are rejected.\n\nVerification: source inspection confirms the shared CallId path; `cargo fmt\n--all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused Cargo checks could not\nstart because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Separate consumer and provider compatibility classes\n\n`working tree` · area: service contract update compatibility\n\nBidirectional contract diffs now expose an independent\n`CompatibilityClassification` containing the consumer and provider result\nclasses. The classification preserves asymmetric changes such as additive state\nfor consumers that is breaking for providers, while retaining each direction's\nfull change list for diagnostics.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo checks could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Negotiate service feature groups per provider\n\n`working tree` · area: service contract capability and provider selection\n\nContracts now compile explicit `capabilities.featureGroups` entries with\nrequired/optional semantics and normalized capability lists. The interface\nregistry and immutable catalog track provider feature advertisements per\nprovider, enable matching groups, tolerate unavailable optional groups, and\nreject providers missing required groups. Lookup diagnostics explain required\nfeature-group gaps, and compatibility diffs classify optional additions as\nadditive and required additions as breaking.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo checks could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Generate service contract authoring artifacts\n\n`working tree` · area: contract tooling and Luau authoring\n\nThe compiled contract now generates deterministic Luau consumer type modules,\nprovider skeletons with explicit `start(self)`, in-memory mocks with call\nrecording, and standalone Markdown documentation. All four outputs consume the\nsame normalized schemas, operation policy, behavioral metadata, fingerprints,\nand provenance; generation returns strings and does not write files.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo checks could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Publish immutable compiled service contracts\n\n`working tree` · area: service contract compilation and catalog authority\n\nService contracts now compile into an immutable, shared `CompiledContract`\nartifact. It owns canonical identity, normalized recursive schemas, unique\ndeclaration symbols, operation capability policy, behavioral transport metadata,\nstable schema/policy/behavior fingerprints, and declaration provenance. Mutable\nregistration and immutable catalog snapshots publish the same `Arc` artifact;\nresolutions retain a raw compatibility view for callers still migrating.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo checks could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Remove the transitional service registry\n\n`working tree` · area: service authority and shell state\n\nThe unused `ServiceRegistry`, `ServiceEntry`, and `ServiceError` second model\nwere removed. The shell no longer carries an untyped TypeId/Any backend store;\ncontract/provider registration and resolution use the generation-stamped\n`InterfaceRegistry`/`ResolvedServiceCatalog` path exclusively.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo checks could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Canonicalize service contract identities\n\n`working tree` · area: service contract identity and tooling indexes\n\nCompiling a contract now canonicalizes its interface identity and rejects an\nempty identity. Runtime registries canonicalize manually constructed contracts\nand providers at registration, while graph declarations, providers, frontend\nrequirements, active-provider selections, compatibility maps, diagnostics, and\nLSP contract/shape indexes use the same canonical key. Graph and LSP lookups\nalso canonicalize aliases at their public boundaries.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Diff executable service contracts in both directions\n\n`working tree` · area: service contract compatibility and update planning\n\nCompatibility diffs now inspect interface identity/version, recursive named\ntypes, event payload additions, and transport behavior (`coalesce` and\n`stateBinding`). Consumer compatibility and provider compatibility are checked\nin opposite directions, with optional removals remaining compatible while\nrequired additions can be provider-breaking. Revision-only update planning now\nloads module-relative external contracts from the candidate Git revision before\nclassification, and the CLI reports provider-side refusals separately.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Deliver generation-safe availability transitions\n\n`working tree` · area: backend lifecycle and service event routing\n\nProvider identity and terminal status now use one active-generation check for\nbackend state updates, interface events, command results, and lifecycle\nmessages. Late messages from replaced or stopped providers are discarded even\nwhen the runtime slot has already been removed. Explicit runtime stops and\nfailures publish `available=false` and the health event through the ordinary\nservice delivery path; the canonical state cache is updated before observers\nare notified, and duplicate availability payloads do not replay the state.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Gate provider activation on validated readiness\n\n`working tree` · area: backend lifecycle, provider switching, and profile activation\n\nBackend runtimes now remain private until they report `Running` and, for\nstateful contracts, emit a valid initial state snapshot. This gate covers\nstartup, supervised restarts, live provider changes, and profile candidates.\nPrepared snapshots are buffered and replayed once after the runtime becomes\nactive; invalid snapshots abort the candidate and preserve the current provider\nand state. Stateless contracts still activate on lifecycle readiness, and\navailability health is published only after the prepared runtime is committed.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests could not start because the local registry lacks `sha2` and network\naccess is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Enforce recursive service contract schemas\n\n`working tree` · area: service contract compilation and runtime validation\n\nInterface type expressions now validate complete named-type graphs, including\narrays, optional presence/null semantics, and the builtin `Result` shape;\nrecursive named-type cycles are rejected during contract validation. The shell\nuses the same matcher for state snapshots, event payloads, direct method\ninputs, and provider method outputs. Invalid state preserves the last-known-\ngood snapshot, invalid events are dropped, malformed inputs never reach a\nbackend queue, and invalid provider results settle the call as a contract\nfailure. Luau method proxies enforce positional arity and argument types while\nrecognizing only the actual proxy table for colon-call self handling.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
