ion.\\n155:- [ ] Preserve the previous discrete value during visibility transitions until the transition completes.\\n156:- [ ] Propagate validated per-keyframe easing through component parsing, shell state, and animation sampling.\\n157:- [ ] Keep interaction policy in a renderer-neutral frame/state-machine contract with typed decisions and dirty outputs.\\n158:- [ ] Implement `box-shadow` parsing with structured errors or reject it before the public animation API.\\n159:- [ ] Give animation instances stable identity and explicit replacement, cancellation, and reversal semantics.\\n160:- [ ] Introduce an `InteractionFrame` shared by input, state, style invalidation, layout, animation, paint, and semantics.\\n166:- [ ] Reject absolute, traversal, and symlinked frontend entrypoint/import paths outside the module root.\\n167:- [ ] Keep service payloads Rust-owned unless the consumer has the resolved read capability; event subscriptions alone must not expose state.\\n168:- [ ] Reload primary and contribution roots together as one atomic catalog generation.\\n169:- [ ] Validate contribution roots against interface requirements, availability, and version ranges.\\n170:- [ ] Validate root and nested expression scopes uniformly using parser/runtime symbol tables and source spans.\\n171:- [ ] Compile expressions once into shared semantics so preview, live, translation, and composition paths behave identically.\\n172:- [ ] Split the frontend host into a renderer-neutral ABI and shell adapters with typed capability-scoped effects.\\n173:- [ ] Build one reverse dependency graph over primary and contribution roots for invalidation.\\n174:- [ ] Scope local component aliases by owner and canonical source, rejecting collisions.\\n175:- [ ] Replace line-oriented Luau symbol discovery with parser/compiler metadata or remove it as a source of truth.\\n176:- [ ] Make expression scanning UTF-8 safe and diagnose non-ASCII input instead of panicking.\\n177:- [ ] Publish runtime props transactionally so Rust and Luau cannot diverge after a failed update.\\n178:- [ ] Preserve typed diagnostic categories and source spans through AST, compiler, shell, LSP, and debug paths.\\n179:- [ ] Prevent stale catalog rollback from overwriting a newer generation using a coordinator or compare-and-swap.\\n180:- [ ] Enforce distinct popover and overflow child-surface lifecycle, focus, dismissal, placement, and ownership semantics.\\n181:- [ ] Dispatch frontend `mount` and `unmount` hooks in every initialization, reload, deactivation, and replacement path.\\n182:- [ ] Contain expression/runtime failures with last-known-good trees or bounded error placeholders and actionable diagnostics.\\n183:- [ ] Publish normalized public-prop schemas and validate imported/contribution props at the import boundary.\\n184:- [ ] Reject local/module import alias collisions or resolve them through one typed import namespace.\\n185:- [ ] Introduce a coherent revisioned `FrontendFrame` boundary for tree, catalog, runtime, services, invalidation, diagnostics, and effects.\\n186:- [ ] Emit immutable compiled frontend revisions and authorize typed effects only when catalog/runtime revisions still match.\\n192:- [ ] Enforce one sandbox/resource policy for every Luau realm, including instruction, memory, output, queue, storage, and child-process budgets.\\n193:- [ ] Keep service state Rust-owned, generation-aware, and capability-filtered instead of exposing shared globals.\\n194:- [ ] Route every backend early return, callback failure, stop, and crash through idempotent cleanup and one terminal lifecycle record.\\n195:- [ ] Make unsubscribe-safe event iteration and independent subscriber failure reporting explicit.\\n196:- [ ] Give stream subprocesses stable identities, bounded queues, exit events, awaited reaping, and shutdown semantics.\\n197:- [ ] Move `mesh.exec` off the async backend loop and enforce cancellation, deadlines, executable policy, and output limits.\\n198:- [ ] Replace basename executable grants with canonical path/argument capability policy.\\n199:- [ ] Move default runtime storage to secure durable XDG state with permissions, quotas, atomic recovery, and revisioned writers.\\n200:- [ ] Make backend command dispatch typed, correlated, transactional, coalescable, generation-aware, and bounded.\\n201:- [ ] Gate event and side-effect queues through one typed authorization/resource boundary before acceptance.\\n202:- [ ] Represent locale as a host-owned per-context cell updated with the translation snapshot.\\n203:- [ ] Treat Luau `nil` writes as explicit deletions in Rust state and dependency invalidation.\\n204:- [ ] Restrict provider event publication to provider-owned handles and isolate subscriber callback failures.\\n205:- [ ] Preserve one stable backend `self` and event/storage handles for each runtime generation.\\n206:- [ ] Publish validated initial provider state before atomically marking the provider ready.\\n207:- [ ] Compile and swap a fresh Luau environment on reload, preserving only explicit durable storage.\\n208:- [ ] Stage backend top-level execution so host side effects cannot escape a failed `start(self)`.\\n209:- [ ] Bound command/event ingress, JSON depth/bytes, event counts, and aggregate runtime resource budgets.\\n210:- [ ] Separate effective read and control grants and enforce them through both proxy and shell paths.\\n211:- [ ] Reconcile changed poll intervals after every stream callback.\\n212:- [ ] Return recoverable host-installation errors instead of panicking during backend setup.\\n213:- [ ] Introduce a per-module `RuntimeSession` combining realm, host, resource broker, lifecycle, state, supervisor, health, backoff, and quarantine.\\n219:- [ ] Make `PixelCanvasSession` storage-safe so mapped drawing surfaces cannot outlive backing allocations.\\n220:- [ ] Lower asymmetric four-edge borders and four-corner radii correctly.\\n221:- [ ] Use one cumulative affine transform/clip model across paint, damage, blur, descendants, and interaction.\\n222:- [ ] Lower node opacity and blend mode as isolated compositing groups instead of per primitive.\\n223:- [ ] Include paint-order/topology changes in display-list generations and stable equal-z ordering.\\n224:- [ ] Unify dirty contracts and paint signatures for all content/style fields, including controls, text, icons, and variables.\\n225:- [ ] Include font/resource revisions in text style painting and all glyph/font/text cache keys.\\n226:- [ ] Make backdrop blur an explicit renderer/backend capability with validated fallback behavior.\\n227:- [ ] Use one fractional-scale rounding policy across layout, buffer, paint, copy, and protocol damage.\\n228:- [ ] Preserve release batch/barrier metrics in diagnostics and debug telemetry.\\n229:- [ ] Validate caller lineage before trusting generation shortcuts.\\n230:- [ ] Include resource revisions in retained-present decisions and cache invalidation.\\n231:- [ ] Preserve pending damage and avoid acknowledging unshown frames after presentation errors.\\n232:- [ ] Move resource decode and rasterization off the frame thread through a bounded resource broker.\\n233:- [ ] Enforce byte- and dimension-based cache budgets for decoded assets, fonts, glyphs, text, Skia, PixelBuffer, and SHM allocations.\\n234:- [ ] Introduce a typed frame paint plan with immutable inputs, topology, transforms, effect regions, replay spans, and exact logical/device damage.\\n240:- [ ] Enforce the author-only `promotable` guard for settings, IPC, and live role changes.\\n241:- [ ] Remove or formally protect `promotable` from user-overridable/ejected settings.\\n242:- [ ] Validate manifest surface enums and role constraints with canonical parsers before graph resolution.\\n243:- [ ] Include blur and window decorations in semantic presentation change detection.\\n244:- [ ] Route settings-driven role reloads through the same transactional transition supervisor as explicit promotion.\\n245:- [ ] Share role-field metadata across manifest diagnostics, settings validation, ejection, and protocol lowering.\\n246:- [ ] Preserve localization identity and distinguish effective values from overrides during configuration ejection.\\n247:- [ ] Use typed unmeasured/content/surface/wire extents at the shell/presentation boundary.\\n248:- [ ] Replace split surface field lists with a revisioned semantic policy diff and generation.\\n249:- [ ] Build the policy compiler producing declared contracts, effective snapshots, and typed transition plans.\\n255:- [ ] Return typed create/configure/present/lost outcomes, cache only accepted generations, and retain damage for missing surfaces.\\n256:- [ ] Route close, dismiss, parent destruction, role replacement, and connection loss through one idempotent teardown supervisor.\\n257:- [ ] Replace incomplete presentation hashes and warm region caches with typed semantic diffs and object/configure/frame generations.\\n258:- [ ] Preserve click-grab seat and serial identity through input normalization, popup requests, and one-shot configuration.\\n259:- [ ] Gate popup reposition by negotiated protocol version and validate popup role, parent, identity, and reparenting.\\n260:- [ ] Use one authoritative logical extent for paint, buffer validation, viewport, regions, attach, and queries.\\n261:- [ ] Commit opaque, blur, and other surface-state changes even when pixel damage is empty.\\n262:- [ ] Separate frame-callback waiting from buffer-release backpressure and prevent hot retry loops.\\n263:- [ ] Make input ownership per seat and cancel pointer, touch, gesture, focus, and repeat transactions during teardown.\\n264:- [ ] Validate buffer length/stride/scale, propagate attach/region errors, expose connection loss, and reap clipboard children.\\n265:- [ ] Replace the recorder backend with a deterministic protocol-state lifecycle simulator plus a focused live compositor matrix.\\n266:- [ ] Add full pointer-button identity and IME/text-input-v3 support while preserving normalized Escape behavior.\\n267:- [ ] Build the transactional, capability-aware presentation engine with version reporting, reactive popups, multi-output membership, per-seat input, and shared SHM/dmabuf/GPU frame contracts.\\n273:- [ ] Replace split profile/runtime mutation with one immutable activation plan and atomic runtime-generation commit.\\n274:- [ ] Reconcile backend enable/disable and every graph delta through the same activation coordinator.\\n275:- [ ] Tag backend tasks, bridges, messages, events, results, and restart deadlines with activation generations and provider epochs.\\n276:- [ ] Make frontend/backend stop, unmount, storage flush, worker join, and shutdown cleanup explicit and idempotent.\\n277:- [ ] Give detached workers owned wake handles and lifecycle guards that outlive the eventfd until join.\\n278:- [ ] Isolate component/runtime callback, tick, build, render, and reload failures with placeholders, diagnostics, and quarantine.\\n279:- [ ] Replace static startup watching with a managed generation-aware watch set and bounded polling fallback.\\n280:- [ ] Process CoreRequest effects through one fair bounded scheduler with causal budgets and cycle detection.\\n281:- [ ] Publish provider unavailable/recovery transitions from committed provider generations.\\n282:- [ ] Route control-plane writes through declared durable revisions and ordered settings/theme/locale effect batches.\\n283:- [ ] Distinguish intentional legacy/no-profile operation from invalid configured graph/profile recovery.\\n284:- [ ] Connect package journal commit/rollback to runtime activation so disk and live state share one recoverable transaction.\\n285:- [ ] Introduce `ActiveSnapshot` with candidate preview in hidden surfaces and an explicit quiescing-to-stopped shutdown state machine.\\n291:- [ ] Make uninstall path-safe and reject traversal/symlink escapes before recursive deletion.\\n292:- [ ] Make package mutations atomic, journaled, crash-recoverable, and failure-injection tested.\\n293:- [ ] Make live profile switching use typed acknowledgements and exact-generation recovery.\\n294:- [ ] Make CLI and shell use one package ownership and transaction contract.\\n295:- [ ] Refresh one canonical graph-authoring snapshot for CLI, doctor, LSP, and runtime consumers.\\n296:- [ ] Generate LSP manifest/schema validation from runtime contracts instead of duplicated under-approximations.\\n297:- [ ] Convert all LSP positions to UTF-16 code units at the protocol boundary.\\n298:- [ ] Make `--replace` and CLI flags enforce their documented typed behavior.\\n299:- [ ] Make LSP analysis syntax-aware with recoverable partial ASTs and useful mid-edit diagnostics.\\n300:- [ ] Replace heuristic Luau/JSON scanners with standards-compliant parsers and source-span data.\\n301:- [ ] Support workspace-folder-only initialization and versioned `didChange` refresh generations.\\n302:- [ ] Select manifest flavors from parsed structure, not textual substring checks.\\n303:- [ ] Make hover consume the current registry and expose service field/command documentation.\\n304:- [ ] Restrict definition resolution to existing module-contained imports.\\n305:- [ ] Preserve Unicode JSON escapes, registry generations, and secure import provenance in authoring diagnostics.\\n315:- [ ] Close module filesystem escapes before any package mutation or source\\n318:- [ ] Make installed-graph activation fail closed and build catalogs/provider\\n321:- [ ] Replace the duplicate CLI/shell package implementations with one locked,\\n324:- [ ] Enforce required/optional module dependencies, module/interface version\\n327:- [ ] Make the canonical `module.json` loader the only production path; legacy\\n330:- [ ] Make module lifecycle and health authoritative across graph, frontend, and\\n333:- [ ] Align the lock schema with the specification and populate dependency and\\n336:- [ ] Move the remaining built-in debug and theme/locale service behavior\\n340:- [ ] **Deferred — unify the four contribution schemas.** Theme, icons, i18n,\\n349:- [ ] Remove shared `__mesh_svc_*` Luau state: keep service payloads in a\\n352:- [ ] Replace the additive interface registry with one immutable, atomic\\n355:- [ ] Compile and enforce complete contracts end to end: canonical unique names,\\n358:- [ ] Make service methods correlated request/response transactions with typed\\n361:- [ ] Gate provider/profile commits on validated readiness and buffered initial\\n364:- [ ] Diff the complete compiled contract in consumer and provider directions,\\n370:- [ ] Make graph-authorized theme descriptors the only catalog/loader, with\\n373:- [ ] Make theme selection, profile switching, graph changes, and hot reload one\\n376:- [ ] Share the restricted CSS/token/keyframe lowering path between themes and\\n379:- [ ] Complete `mesh.theme` and settings with modes, sparse token overrides,\\n385:- [ ] Replace per-surface locale engines and the cross-module global key pool\\n388:- [ ] Make locale selection a durable revisioned settings/profile transaction:\\n391:- [ ] Compile bounded typed catalogs with per-entry diagnostics, interpolation,\\n394:- [ ] Route templates, Luau, manifests, props, generated settings, and debug data\\n397:- [ ] Drive locale CLI/LSP/doctor, extraction, missing-key and provenance tooling\\n403:- [ ] Replace discovery-time global resource registration with one immutable,\\n406:- [ ] Make icon resolution deterministic and complete: canonical owner-scoped\\n409:- [ ] Complete font-pack runtime support with logical and pack-qualified roles,\\n412:- [ ] Unify XDG and font discovery into a refreshable host catalog; propagate\\n415:- [ ] Remove legacy icon config and discovery authorities, and drive bounded\\n421:- [ ] Replace lossy `.mesh` block extraction and ad-hoc template preprocessing\\n424:- [ ] Make component compilation resolve imports per owner, enforce module-root\\n427:- [ ] Make the `<props>` contract one normalized typed value pipeline: reject\\n