{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"test -f .codex-continuation.md && sed -n '1,240p' .codex-continuation.md || true\"","aggregated_output":"# MESH continuation handoff\n\n## Objective\n\nWork through the documented project backlog in priority order, implementing\ncoherent scoped increments, running relevant tests, and continuing while usage\nremains. Avoid unrelated changes.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Repository guidance is in `AGENTS.md`; architecture/spec were read:\n  `docs/architecture/overview.md` and `docs/spec/README.md`.\n- `docs/BACKLOG.md` is the sole open-work list. Completed work must be removed\n  from it and recorded in `.planning/log/2026-08.md`; `.planning/STATUS.md`\n  describes current work. Logs are append-only.\n- Preserve the existing dirty worktree. Do not reset, checkout, or overwrite\n  unrelated user changes. Use `apply_patch` for edits.\n- MESH is a Rust, Wayland-only shell framework; service behavior belongs in\n  generic runtime/module paths, not hardcoded service-specific Rust policy.\n\n## Completed in this run\n\nThe highest-priority open service-contract item was split after landing its\ntransport slice. Shell-admitted backend service commands now have a unique\n`CallId` that survives throttling/coalescing and returns in a correlated\nterminal result. Added outcomes: `completed`, `failed`, `superseded`,\n`timed_out`, and `cancelled`. The shell updates the matching debug transaction\ninstead of appending an uncorrelated result. A backend call-control registry\nsupports a 100 ms pre-execution deadline and queued cancellation; synchronous\nLuau handlers are intentionally not interrupted.\n\nThe backlog line was narrowed from:\n\n`Make service methods correlated awaitable transactions with call IDs, deadlines, cancellation, and terminal outcomes.`\n\nto the still-open remainder:\n\n`Expose correlated service calls to Luau as awaitable tickets with caller-driven cancellation and completion delivery.`\n\nThe second service item, optimistic state settlement/rollback, remains open.\n\nExisting dirty work discovered at the start was preserved and treated as\nin-scope: signed module provenance/trust-policy verification and\nRust-owned, capability-filtered per-context service snapshots. Their records\nare already in the August log and status file.\n\n## Repository and git state\n\n- Working directory: `/home/kolby/projects/mesh`\n- Branch: `main`\n- HEAD at the start of this run: `38466b5b` (`feat: enforce module trust tier policy`)\n- No commit was created in this run.\n- Worktree is dirty with pre-existing edits plus the service transport slice;\n  preserve all of them. `codex-loop.log` is untracked and belongs to the\n  existing automation state.\n\n## Files changed in this run\n\n- `crates/core/runtime/backend/src/lib.rs` — `CallId`, terminal outcomes,\n  call-control registry, correlated command/supersession results, tests.\n- `crates/core/foundation/debug/src/lib.rs` — `MethodCallEntry.call_id`.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/backend/spawn.rs` — bridge call IDs/outcomes.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/debug.rs` — correlate result with the\n  queued debug entry.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/mod.rs` — handle correlated results.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/request.rs` — allocate IDs, register\n  bounded calls, preserve IDs through throttling, and return IDs in receipts.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/theme.rs` — ID for the internal theme\n  command.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/types.rs` — result fields and throttled-command\n  ID storage.\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/commands.rs` and\n  `crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/service_contract.rs` — focused coverage.\n- `docs/BACKLOG.md`, `.planning/STATUS.md`,\n  `.planning/log/2026-08.md` — tracking the completed slice and remaining\n  caller-facing work.\n\nOther dirty files were present before this run; inspect `git status --short`\nand `git diff --stat` before touching them.\n\n## Architectural decisions\n\n- `CallId` lives in `mesh-core-backend`, avoiding a scripting/backend cycle;\n  shell and backend share the same transport identity.\n- Existing service payload ABI and command payloads remain unchanged.\n- Coalesced older calls produce explicit `superseded` results rather than\n  disappearing silently.\n- Deadline/cancellation applies before synchronous Luau handler execution;\n  hard interruption of a running handler is not safe and was deliberately not\n  attempted.\n- The shell currently creates IDs at service dispatch. The frontend proxy does\n  not yet receive completion data, so this is a transport/debug increment, not\n  completion of the full awaitable API.\n\n## Tests and results\n\nPassed:\n\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nAttempted but blocked before compilation:\n\n- `cargo test --offline -p mesh-core-backend --lib call_control_produces_terminal_timeout_and_cancel_outcomes`\n- `cargo test --offline -p mesh-core-shell --lib service_command_dispatch_records_debug_method_call`\n- `cargo test --offline -p mesh-core-shell --lib coalescable_service_commands_use_a_backend_cost_budget`\n- Earlier focused scripting/module tests were blocked for the same reason.\n\nBlocker: the local Cargo registry cache has no `sha2` entry required by\n`mesh-core-module`, and network access is unavailable. Do not represent the\nfocused tests as passing until dependencies are available.\n\n## Unresolved problems\n\n- Luau needs an awaitable service-call ticket with completion delivery back to\n  the originating script context/instance, plus caller-driven cancellation.\n- The proxy publication path currently has no caller-visible correlated result;\n  design the context/instance routing before changing `PublishedEvent` or\n  `CoreRequest` broadly.\n- Optimistic `stateBinding` writes are still keyed only by interface/field and\n  need CallId/provider-generation-aware settle/rollback behavior, including\n  timeout, cancellation, failure, and provider replacement.\n- Cargo test execution remains blocked by the missing offline `sha2` crate.\n\n## Exact next steps\n\n1. On resume, inspect `git status --short` and the focused diffs; preserve all\n   pre-existing edits and verify the handoff files were not duplicated.\n2. When the dependency is available, rerun formatting/diff checks and the\n   three focused tests above, then run the relevant backend/shell service test\n   slices.\n3. Implement the remaining top backlog item: propagate a stable call identity\n   from the Luau proxy through `PublishedEvent`/`CoreRequest` (or an equivalent\n   typed request envelope), route terminal results to the originating context,\n   expose an awaitable/pollable Luau ticket, and expose caller cancellation.\n   Add out-of-order, timeout, cancellation, supersession, and completion\n   delivery regressions before removing that backlog line.\n4. Record the completed item in `.planning/log/2026-08.md`, update\n   `.planning/STATUS.md`, and remove only the fully completed backlog line.\n5. Continue with the next item, optimistic state transaction settlement and\n   rollback, without broadening into unrelated service-catalog work.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
