{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"git status --short && git diff --stat && git diff -- docs/BACKLOG.md .planning/STATUS.md .planning/log/2026-08.md | sed -n '1,280p'\"","aggregated_output":" M .codex-continuation.md\n M .planning/STATUS.md\n M .planning/log/2026-08.md\n M Cargo.lock\n M codex-loop.log\n M crates/core/foundation/config/Cargo.toml\n M crates/core/foundation/config/src/lib.rs\n M crates/core/foundation/locale/src/lib.rs\n M crates/core/foundation/theme/src/lib.rs\n M crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/runtime/context.rs\n M crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/runtime/helpers.rs\n M crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/runtime/host_api.rs\n M crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/state.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/rendering/mod.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/runtime.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/shell_component/mod.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/tests/interaction/keybinds.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/mod.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/profile.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/debug.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/mod.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/service_state.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/theme.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/surface_layout.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/debug.rs\n M crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/theme.rs\n M docs/BACKLOG.md\n .codex-continuation.md                             |  158 +--\n .planning/STATUS.md                                |   23 +-\n .planning/log/2026-08.md                           |  130 +++\n Cargo.lock                                         |    1 +\n codex-loop.log                                     |  755 +++++++++++++++\n crates/core/foundation/config/Cargo.toml           |    1 +\n crates/core/foundation/config/src/lib.rs           |    6 +\n crates/core/foundation/locale/src/lib.rs           | 1015 ++++++++++++++++++--\n crates/core/foundation/theme/src/lib.rs            |  371 ++++++-\n .../scripting/src/context/runtime/context.rs       |   18 +-\n .../scripting/src/context/runtime/helpers.rs       |   33 +-\n .../scripting/src/context/runtime/host_api.rs      |    9 +-\n crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/state.rs |   18 +-\n .../shell/src/shell/component/rendering/mod.rs     |   12 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/runtime.rs   |   61 +-\n .../src/shell/component/shell_component/mod.rs     |   12 +-\n .../shell/component/tests/interaction/keybinds.rs  |   18 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs           |   54 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/mod.rs                 |    4 +\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/profile.rs             |   57 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/debug.rs       |    5 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/mod.rs         |    7 +-\n .../core/shell/src/shell/runtime/service_state.rs  |   25 +\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/theme.rs       |  123 ++-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/surface_layout.rs      |   36 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/debug.rs         |   10 +-\n crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/theme.rs         |   80 +-\n docs/BACKLOG.md                                    |    8 +-\n 28 files changed, 2706 insertions(+), 344 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/.planning/STATUS.md b/.planning/STATUS.md\nindex 009caa7f..4d58b819 100644\n--- a/.planning/STATUS.md\n+++ b/.planning/STATUS.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Status\n \n-**Updated:** 2026-08-21\n+**Updated:** 2026-08-22\n \n This page describes the present. History lives in [`log/`](log/); open work\n lives in [`docs/BACKLOG.md`](../docs/BACKLOG.md).\n@@ -23,7 +23,26 @@ state/class rules execute through the same element matcher, and malformed\n theme CSS is rejected with bounded declaration parsing. Theme and component\n keyframes now share runtime lowering, token aliases resolve transitively with\n cycle diagnostics, and computed style snapshots carry inherited custom\n-properties. The rendered theme snapshot is the next theme item.\n+properties. The rendered theme snapshot is authoritative for the shell's\n+mode, color scheme, contrast, effective tokens, provenance, and revisioned\n+`ThemeChanged`/`TokenChanged` interface events; provider mirrors cannot replace\n+it. ThemeEngine now retains immutable active snapshot identity and rejects\n+ambiguous registrations. Explicit manual, system-following, and scheduled mode\n+policies now use the same transaction path; policy changes are persisted in the\n+theme snapshot and trigger the same revisioned event/invalidation flow. Locale\n+catalogs now expose explicit\n+module/core translators: templates, Luau, manifests, debug metadata, and\n+generated component settings use the owning module without global key leakage.\n+Locale selection is now normalized and immutable at the snapshot boundary:\n+BCP 47 tags derive parent and terminal fallback chains, direction and revision\n+are published with the locale service state, and invalid runtime tags are\n+rejected. Typed catalog compilation now preserves valid siblings, validates\n+placeholder parity, and resolves bounded plural/select entries in Rust and\n+Luau. LocaleEngine now publishes revisioned immutable catalog Arcs with an\n+explicit replacement seam; the remaining snapshot work is wiring that seam\n+through graph/profile/reload preparation and last-known-good commits. Surface\n+mounts now prepare all graph catalogs into a candidate and commit one catalog\n+Arc only when asset reads succeed.\n \n The first four Section 2 items are complete. Package commits publish\n validated module trees into a read-only SHA-256 object store and activate\ndiff --git a/.planning/log/2026-08.md b/.planning/log/2026-08.md\nindex 68e0d9a9..38e98a5c 100644\n--- a/.planning/log/2026-08.md\n+++ b/.planning/log/2026-08.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,135 @@\n # August 2026\n \n+## 2026-08-22 — Prepare graph locale catalogs before surface commit\n+\n+`working tree` · area: surface catalog lifecycle\n+\n+Frontend surfaces now compile graph catalogs into a fresh locale candidate and\n+replace their catalog Arc only after all catalog assets are readable. An asset\n+read/parse failure retains the prior catalog snapshot while valid structured\n+entries continue to produce per-entry diagnostics.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and\n+`git diff --check` pass. The focused locale suite passed 9 tests before this\n+shell-only wiring; workspace compilation remains blocked by pre-existing\n+service/module/scripting errors before the shell crate.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Establish immutable locale catalog snapshots\n+\n+`working tree` · area: catalog snapshot ownership\n+\n+`LocaleEngine` now stores catalogs behind a revisioned immutable\n+`LocaleCatalogSnapshot` Arc. Catalog loads use copy-on-write preparation, and\n+callers can atomically replace the catalog pointer while readers retain the\n+previous last-known-good snapshot. The shell/graph/profile coordinator still\n+needs to adopt this seam; that remaining work stays open in the backlog.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n+(9 tests), `git diff --check` passed. The final formatting check was retried\n+after the Nix daemon socket was temporarily unavailable; earlier focused\n+format checks pass for the same working tree.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Compile typed locale entries without sibling loss\n+\n+`working tree` · area: typed catalogs and shared message rendering\n+\n+Locale catalog loading now compiles bounded string, plural, and select entries\n+independently. Invalid keys, malformed placeholders, inconsistent variant\n+placeholders, unknown plural categories, and oversized entries produce\n+per-entry diagnostics while valid siblings remain available. Rust translators\n+share interpolation and plural/select resolution, and Luau `t(key, values)`\n+uses the same compiled entries. Graph catalog loading now accepts structured\n+JSON instead of rejecting an entire file at the first plural object.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n+(8 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff\n+--check` pass. The scripting/shell workspace remains blocked by pre-existing\n+closure ownership and module graph compilation errors before shell compilation.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Normalize locale selection into revisioned snapshots\n+\n+`working tree` · area: locale selection and service state\n+\n+Added immutable `LocaleSelection` snapshots with canonical BCP 47 casing,\n+derived script/region parents, explicit terminal fallback, RTL/LTR direction,\n+and monotonic revisions. Locale changes now replace the prior chain instead of\n+accumulating stale locales; invalid runtime tags are rejected. The shell\n+publishes the normalized chain, direction, and revision, and retained\n+components adopt the same selection snapshot.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n+(7 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff\n+--check` pass. Workspace compilation remains blocked by pre-existing errors in\n+the service, module, and scripting crates before shell compilation.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Replace global locale lookup with owner-scoped translators\n+\n+`working tree` · area: localization ownership and consumption\n+\n+`LocaleEngine` no longer merges module catalogs into a shared translation\n+pool. It now exposes explicit module and core translator handles; module\n+translators resolve only their owner’s catalogs. Template variable stores,\n+Luau i18n maps, manifest text, debug metadata, and generated composition prop\n+settings all use the corresponding owner-scoped handle. Existing keybind/debug\n+fixtures were migrated to module-owned catalogs, and cross-module/core leakage\n+is covered by locale tests.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n+(4 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff\n+--check` pass. The scripting/shell compile remains blocked by the pre-existing\n+`InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n+`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Route theme mode policies through candidate preparation\n+\n+`working tree` · area: theme mode selection and settings\n+\n+Theme settings now support explicit `manual`, `follow_system`, and\n+`scheduled` policies. A pure selector validates declared modes, matches system\n+color-scheme metadata, resolves local clock schedules, and rejects malformed,\n+unknown, or duplicate entries. Graph theme preparation and reload fingerprint\n+checks use that selector, so policy transitions enter the same candidate\n+composition, invalidation, and revisioned event path as manual changes.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed\n+(23 tests), `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-config --lib` passed\n+(41 tests), and formatting/diff checks pass. The focused shell suite remains\n+blocked by the pre-existing `InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n+`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Make active theme snapshots immutable and identities deterministic\n+\n+`working tree` · area: theme snapshot identity and catalog registration\n+\n+ThemeEngine now keeps an `Arc` of the active immutable snapshot and refreshes it\n+only after controlled active-theme edits or replacement commits. The unrestricted\n+mutable active-theme accessor was removed; duplicate, whitespace-ambiguous, and\n+empty available-theme identities are rejected before registration, while graph\n+registration reports the rejection and continues safely.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed\n+(21 tests); `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. The\n+focused shell suite remains blocked by the pre-existing\n+`InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n+`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Publish the authoritative rendered theme snapshot\n+\n+`working tree` · area: theme snapshot state and events\n+\n+The shell now publishes the rendered theme snapshot as the sole `mesh.theme`\n+state source and declares shell-owned `ThemeChanged` and `TokenChanged`\n+interface events. Theme changes carry mode, color scheme, contrast, revision,\n+the complete effective token/provenance maps, and deterministic changed-token\n+records; individual token events carry the same revision and winning-layer\n+provenance. Provider state cannot overwrite the rendered snapshot.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed\n+(20 tests); `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. The\n+focused shell suite is blocked by a pre-existing compile error in\n+`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229` (`InterfaceProvider`\n+cannot be dereferenced).\n+\n ## 2026-08-21 — Retain last-known-good theme candidates\n \n `4d11e431` · area: theme/profile/reload transactions\ndiff --git a/docs/BACKLOG.md b/docs/BACKLOG.md\nindex 93dd996a..7810f64a 100644\n--- a/docs/BACKLOG.md\n+++ b/docs/BACKLOG.md\n@@ -48,18 +48,12 @@ the monthly log, so they are intentionally absent from the open backlog.\n ### 4. Themes\n \n [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/04-themes/improvements.md)\n-- [ ] Make the rendered theme snapshot authoritative for mode, color scheme, contrast, tokens, provenance, and revisioned events.\n-- [ ] Make theme snapshots immutable and reject duplicate or ambiguous identities for deterministic caching.\n-- [ ] Add explicit manual, follow-system, and scheduled theme mode policies through the same transaction coordinator.\n \n ### 5. Localization and i18n\n \n [Audit](../.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md)\n \n-- [ ] Replace the global translation pool with owner-scoped translators for templates, scripts, manifests, props, debug data, and settings UI.\n-- [ ] Implement an immutable normalized locale selection with BCP 47 parents, direction, complete fallback chain, and revision.\n-- [ ] Compile bounded typed message/plural/select entries independently with checked placeholders and shared formatting.\n-- [ ] Build one immutable catalog snapshot with atomic graph/profile/selection/reload commits and last-known-good recovery.\n+- [ ] Thread the immutable locale catalog snapshot through atomic graph/profile/selection/reload commits with last-known-good recovery.\n - [ ] Add targeted ordered language-pack chains, per-module defaults, winning-source provenance, and duplicate precedence checks.\n - [ ] Route locale changes through one durable revision-checked settings/profile transaction.\n - [ ] Align `mesh.i18n`, `mesh.locale`, runtime/LSP ABI, and read/write capability enforcement.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
