{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec/07-i18n.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec/07-i18n.md\"","aggregated_output":"# 07 — Localization\n\n> Part of the [MESH Specification](README.md).\n\nLocalization is **module-authored and user-extensible**: every module ships\ntranslations for its own strings; **language packs** layer additional or\nreplacement catalogs on top (ordered multi-active chain, like icon packs);\nthe user picks a locale and fallback chain. Lookups go through the\n`mesh.locale` interface — the same contract-and-registry model as everything\nelse.\n\n**Status: shipped** (catalogs, `t()`, locale switching, fallback,\nmanifest-localized text); language-pack layering and some formatting surface\nare **target** where marked.\n\n## 1. Scoping\n\nTranslations are **scoped by module id**: `results.files` in\n`@mesh/launcher` never collides with `results.files` in another module. This\nis what makes third-party packs safe — they target modules individually.\nInterface modules may also own catalogs (shared domain strings).\n\n## 2. Module-bundled catalogs\n\n```json\n\"mesh\": {\n  \"i18n\": { \"defaultLocale\": \"en\", \"supportedLocales\": [\"en\", \"sk\"] },\n  \"provides\": {\n    \"i18n\": [\n      { \"id\": \"en\", \"locale\": \"en\", \"path\": \"config/i18n/en.json\" },\n      { \"id\": \"sk\", \"locale\": \"sk\", \"path\": \"config/i18n/sk.json\" }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `mesh.i18n.supportedLocales` is install metadata (which language assets an\n  installer may fetch/enable); `defaultLocale` is the module's terminal\n  fallback and belongs in `supportedLocales`.\n- `mesh.provides.i18n` lists the concrete bundled files. Any module kind may\n  bundle catalogs for its own strings.\n\n## 3. Language packs\n\nA `language-pack` module contributes catalogs *for other modules* using the\nsame contribution shape, one entry per target module:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@community/cs-language-pack\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"mesh\": {\n    \"apiVersion\": \"0.1\",\n    \"kind\": \"language-pack\",\n    \"provides\": {\n      \"i18n\": [\n        { \"id\": \"launcher-cs\", \"locale\": \"cs\", \"module\": \"@mesh/launcher\",\n          \"path\": \"translations/@mesh/launcher/cs.json\" },\n        { \"id\": \"panel-cs\", \"locale\": \"cs\", \"module\": \"@mesh/panel\",\n          \"path\": \"translations/@mesh/panel/cs.json\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n*(Status: target — the `module` targeting field and pack layering.)* Multiple\npacks coexist as an ordered chain; catalogs from packs shadow module-bundled\ncatalogs key-by-key. Community translators can localize modules they don't\nown; when a module renames keys, packs targeting it need updates.\n\n## 4. Catalog format\n\nFlat JSON, key → string; dotted keys are organizational, lookup treats them\nas opaque.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"search.placeholder\": \"Hľadať aplikácie\",\n  \"battery.charging\": \"Nabíja sa, {time_to_full}\",\n  \"notifications.count\": {\n    \"_plural\": true,\n    \"one\": \"{count} upozornenie\", \"few\": \"{count} upozornenia\",\n    \"many\": \"{count} upozornení\", \"other\": \"{count} upozornení\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- **Interpolation**: `{name}` substitutes `args.name`; no expression\n  evaluation in strings.\n- **Plurals**: `_plural: true` objects with CLDR categories; `other`\n  required.\n\n## 5. Lookup chain\n\nFor `(module_id, key)`:\n\n1. User-pinned override (settings store; rare, for corrections)\n2. Language packs providing `(module_id, active_locale)`, chain order\n3. Module-bundled catalog for the active locale\n4. Repeat 2–3 for each locale in the user's fallback chain\n5. Module-bundled `defaultLocale` catalog\n6. Visible miss: the key rendered as `!!key` plus a diagnostic\n\nLocale codes are BCP 47; matching is most-specific-first (`sk-SK` satisfies\n`sk`; not vice versa unless the chain says so). User settings\n([08](08-settings.md)):\n\n```json\n\"shell\": { \"locale\": { \"active\": \"sk-SK\", \"chain\": [\"sk-SK\", \"sk\", \"en\"] } }\n```\n\nWhen `chain` is omitted it derives from `active` (drop region → drop script →\n`en`). Changing locale emits `LocaleChanged`; every subscriber refreshes.\n\n## 6. Consumption surfaces\n\n**Scripts** — the i18n library and locale interface:\n\n```luau\nlocal t = import(\"mesh.i18n\", \"t\")\nlocal loc = require(\"mesh.locale\")\n\nlabel = t(\"search.placeholder\")                 -- module-scoped key\nloc.format_number(1234567.89)                    -- \"1 234 567,89\" in sk-SK\nloc.format_date(os.time(), \"short\")\nloc.format_duration(3675)                        -- \"1 h 1 min\"\n```\n\nModules never hand-format numbers/dates/durations — CLDR rules differ per\nlocale. *(Formatting surface beyond `t`: target.)*\n\n**Manifests** — field-local localized text objects wherever a manifest field\nshould be catalog-backed (keybind labels, prop labels):\n\n```json\n\"label\": { \"t\": \"keybind.mute.label\", \"fallback\": \"Mute audio\" }\n```\n\nRaw strings in manifest text fields are literals, never implicit keys.\n`fallback` is required and used when no catalog resolves; misses are\nnon-fatal diagnostics with module id, field path, key, and fallback.\n\n**Props** — `label`/`description`/enum labels in `<props>` are\n`LocalizedText` resolved the same way ([03 §3](03-components.md)). The\ninstalled graph scans `.mesh` sources for `t()` keys and reports missing\ncatalog entries.\n\n## 7. RTL, bidi, and script fallback\n\n- `locale.dir` exposes `\"ltr\"`/`\"rtl\"`; surfaces flip automatically for RTL\n  locales. Authors use logical properties (`margin-inline-start`), not\n  physical ones.\n- Font fallback for scripts the active fonts lack is the renderer's job\n  (cosmic-text); themes may declare script-specific stacks later\n  ([06 §8](06-fonts.md)).\n\n*(Status: target.)*\n\n## 8. Tooling\n\n```\nmesh locale list                    # locales available (bundled + packs)\nmesh locale active                  # current locale + chain\nmesh locale set <code>\nmesh locale which <module> <key>    # which layer supplied the string\nmesh locale missing <module>        # keys with no catalog entry\nmesh locale extract <module>        # translator template with every used key\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
