G.md-52-### 5. Localization and i18n\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-53-\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-54-[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md)\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-55-\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:56:- [ ] Route locale changes through one durable revision-checked settings/profile transaction.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:57:- [ ] Align `mesh.i18n`, `mesh.locale`, runtime/LSP ABI, and read/write capability enforcement.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-58-- [ ] Centralize localized metadata and visible miss handling with owner, fallback, source, and snapshot revision.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-59-- [ ] Open bounded catalogs through contained no-follow source handles and compile them off the shell thread.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:60:- [ ] Drive locale CLI/LSP/extraction/doctor tooling from the canonical graph, and implement or explicitly reject `<i18n>` blocks.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:61:- [ ] Add manual, follow-system, and per-profile locale policies through the same prepare/persist/commit path.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-62-\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-63-### 6. Host resources and icon packs\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-64-\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-65-[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/06-host-resources-and-icon-packs/improvements.md)\n--\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-96-\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-97-[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/08-ui-element-core/improvements.md)\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-98-\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-99-- [ ] Normalize roles, names, descriptions, hidden state, ARIA aliases, focus, relationships, and visibility after child construction and publish the semantic snapshot.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:100:- [ ] Use visible descendant text in accessible-name precedence and preserve hidden-child and locale behavior.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-101-- [ ] Generate one typed pseudo-state table for indexing, mutation, matching, invalidation, diagnostics, and tests.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-102-- [ ] Make compiler inheritance matching consume the actual element state.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-103-- [ ] Make retained layout transactional, preserve last-known-good geometry, and retry after failure.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-104-- [ ] Use one stateful input dispatcher with pointer capture, press-origin identity, activation semantics, focus eligibility, and invalidation output.\n--\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-166-- [ ] Replace basename executable grants with canonical path/argument capability policy.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-167-- [ ] Move default runtime storage to secure durable XDG state with permissions, quotas, atomic recovery, and revisioned writers.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-168-- [ ] Make backend command dispatch typed, correlated, transactional, coalescable, generation-aware, and bounded.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-169-- [ ] Gate event and side-effect queues through one typed authorization/resource boundary before acceptance.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:170:- [ ] Represent locale as a host-owned per-context cell updated with the translation snapshot.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-171-- [ ] Treat Luau `nil` writes as explicit deletions in Rust state and dependency invalidation.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-172-- [ ] Restrict provider event publication to provider-owned handles and isolate subscriber callback failures.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-173-- [ ] Preserve one stable backend `self` and event/storage handles for each runtime generation.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-174-- [ ] Publish validated initial provider state before atomically marking the provider ready.\n--\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-246-- [ ] Isolate component/runtime callback, tick, build, render, and reload failures with placeholders, diagnostics, and quarantine.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-247-- [ ] Replace static startup watching with a managed generation-aware watch set and bounded polling fallback.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-248-- [ ] Process CoreRequest effects through one fair bounded scheduler with causal budgets and cycle detection.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-249-- [ ] Publish provider unavailable/recovery transitions from committed provider generations.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md:250:- [ ] Route control-plane writes through declared durable revisions and ordered settings/theme/locale effect batches.\ndocs/BACKLOG.md-251-- [ ] Distinguish intentional legacy/no-profile 