the chain says so). User settings\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-110-([08](08-settings.md)):\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-111-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-112-```json\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:113:\"shell\": { \"locale\": { \"active\": \"sk-SK\", \"chain\": [\"sk-SK\", \"sk\", \"en\"] } }\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-114-```\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-115-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-116-When `chain` is omitted it derives from `active` (drop region → drop script →\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:117:`en`). Changing locale emits `LocaleChanged`; every subscriber refreshes.\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-118-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-119-## 6. Consumption surfaces\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-120-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:121:**Scripts** — the i18n library and locale interface:\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-122-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-123-```luau\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-124-local t = import(\"mesh.i18n\", \"t\")\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:125:local loc = require(\"mesh.locale\")\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-126-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-127-label = t(\"search.placeholder\")                 -- module-scoped key\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-128-loc.format_number(1234567.89)                    -- \"1 234 567,89\" in sk-SK\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-129-loc.format_date(os.time(), \"short\")\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-130-loc.format_duration(3675)                        -- \"1 h 1 min\"\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-131-```\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-132-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-133-Modules never hand-format numbers/dates/durations — CLDR rules differ per\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:134:locale. *(Formatting surface beyond `t`: target.)*\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-135-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-136-**Manifests** — field-local localized text objects wherever a manifest field\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-137-should be catalog-backed (keybind labels, prop labels):\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-138-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-139-```json\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-140-\"label\": { \"t\": \"keybind.mute.label\", \"fallback\": \"Mute audio\" }\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-141-```\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-142-\n--\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-146-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-147-**Props** — `label`/`description`/enum labels in `<props>` are\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-148-`LocalizedText` resolved the same way ([03 §3](03-components.md)). The\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-149-installed graph scans `.mesh` sources for `t()` keys and reports missing\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-150-catalog entries.\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-151-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-152-## 7. RTL, bidi, and script fallback\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-153-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:154:- `locale.dir` exposes `\"ltr\"`/`\"rtl\"`; surfaces flip automatically for RTL\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:155:  locales. Authors use logical properties (`margin-inline-start`), not\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-156-  physical ones.\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-157-- Font fallback for scripts the active fonts lack is the renderer's job\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-158-  (cosmic-text); themes may declare script-specific stacks later\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-159-  ([06 §8](06-fonts.md)).\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-160-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-161-*(Status: target.)*\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-162-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-163-## 8. Tooling\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-164-\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-165-```\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:166:mesh locale list                    # locales available (bundled + packs)\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:167:mesh locale active                  # current locale + chain\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:168:mesh locale set <code>\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:169:mesh locale which <module> <key>    # which layer supplied the string\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:170:mesh locale missing <module>        # keys with no catalog entry\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md:171:mesh locale extract <module>        # translator template with every used key\ndocs/spec/07-i18n.md-172-```\n--\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-34-rejected experiments were archived to\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-35-`.planning/performance/performance-log.md` on 2026-07-13.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-36-Section letters (A–V) in the performance items below refer to that log.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-37-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-38----\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-39-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-40-## Shell features\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-41-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:42:- [x] Settings module — surface for managing installed modules, active providers, theme, i18n → v1.22. Progress 2026-07-02: added shipped `@mesh/settings` frontend surface (`modules/frontend/settings`) with a right-overlay dialog, graph-backed installed-module list/filter, active-provider binding summary, and live theme/locale controls wired through existing `shell.set-theme` and `mesh.locale.set` paths. `@mesh/quick-settings` now exposes an Open settings action that publishes `shell.show-surface` for `@mesh/settings` and hides the quick-settings popover. The installed graph now auto-discovers the settings module and the fixture test asserts it. Added 2026-07-16: provider rows enumerate enabled alternatives and use a settings-only `shell.set-provider` path that starts the candidate in isolation, keeps the current provider active until readiness, and persists the selection atomically before the live handoff. Module rows apply enable/disable decisions live for both auto-discovery and explicit-inventory root graphs; frontend surfaces are mounted or torn down dynamically, inactive backend graph changes take effect immediately, and configuration is rolled back if graph reload or frontend activation fails. The UI protects itself, the active root layout, active providers, and pending providers from disable actions. Full-shell verification now mounts the shipped surface dynamically, publishes the real debug graph, renders through the shell and presentation pipeline, and asserts configured geometry plus substantial painted output.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-43-- [ ] Popups / overlays — transient surfaces with custom content and dismiss behavior → v1.22\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-44-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-45-### Module architecture friction redesign — 2026-06-19\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-46-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-47-The brainstorm and decision record were folded into\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-48-`docs/spec/01-module-system.md`.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-49-Attacks authoring friction on top of the shipped interface/provider/frontend spine\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-50-(easy / unified / configurable). Selected path: **A+B headline, C/D reframed, F follow-on, E deferred.**\n--\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-54-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-55-### Module system — remaining open follow-ups\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-56-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-57-The 2026-06-18 redesign largely shipped (canonical `module.json` with `mesh.uses`/\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-58-`mesh.provides`/`mesh.implements`, graph as single source of truth, typed graph\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-59-diagnostics for interfaces/icons/i18n/keybinds/capabilities, library modules,\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-60-resource packs). Remaining open work:\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-61-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:62:- [ ] Eliminate service-specific Rust branches where possible. Progress 2026-07-26: command-to-state reactivity is a shell feature — contract methods declare `stateBinding: { field, fromArg }`, and core updates the canonical state for any interface (`pending_bound_service_state`) until the provider confirms it; the `mesh.theme` settings-injection branch became a generic `__shell` context (`{ theme, locale }`) injected into every backend's settings. Remaining: startup-sound path calls the mesh.audio handler directly; debug/profiling paths.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-63-- [ ] Support multiple instances of the same frontend module. Module identity should not be the only surface identity; root graph should support configured instances like two panels or repeated widgets with separate settings/storage scopes.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-64-- [ ] Implement named shell profiles as the starting point for root component\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-65-      instances, surface placement, provider bindings, resources, and\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-66-      profile-scoped overrides.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:67:- [ ] Implement transactional live profile switching that retains identical\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-68-      service instances and leaves the active profile untouched when candidate\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-69-      initialization fails.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-70-- [ ] Add external `contract.json` support with keyed state, method, event, and\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-71-      type objects; compile it into the existing `InterfaceContract` model and\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-72-      generate strict Luau/LSP types.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-73-- [ ] Settings UI generated from contributed schemas by default, with optional custom `settings_ui` entrypoint for advanced modules.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:74:- [ ] Settings/diagnostics UI should show each module's uses/provides graph: required interfaces, active provider, optional interfaces, required icons, native binaries, capabilities, settings namespace, i18n catalogs, keybinds, health. Progress: `mesh.debug.module_graph` payload exists and the debug-inspector Modules tab renders the first entries. Added 2026-07-02: typed graph entries and JSON include required/optional native binaries, keybind action IDs, resolved `interface=provider` pairs, and structured native-binary availability states; the Modules view renders them, correctly handles structured provided-interface records, and filters across IDs, kinds, interfaces, providers, binaries, keybinds, and diagnostics. Binary resolution is shared with installed-graph diagnostics and supports explicit executable paths as well as PATH lookup. Added later 2026-07-02: shipped `@mesh/settings` consumes the same debug graph for end-user module/provider visibility and theme/locale controls. Remaining: per-module customization controls in the full settings UI.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-75-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-76-### Embeddable popovers via `<popover>` surface promotion — 2026-06-21\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-77-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-78-**Problem.** `language-popover` and `theme-selector` are each shipped as a\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-79-_standalone frontend module that owns its own Wayland layer surface_, with\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-80-hardcoded geometry (`width/height/min/max = 112×74`) and hand-computed\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-81-positioning (`shell.position-surface` + `margin_top = -18` math). This is the\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-82-root cause of three observed defects:\n--\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-218-## Performance — open items\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-219-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-220-### Text rendering follow-ups\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-221-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-222-- [x] Improve first-miss ellipsis truncation by using shaped glyph advances\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-223-      instead of binary-search substring measurement.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-224-- [x] Add profiling visibility for text and glyph cache pressure: entry counts,\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-225-      hits, misses, invalidations, and shaping time.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:226:- [x] Add locale-, script-, and direction-sensitive text cases to canonical\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-227-      performance workloads before changing shaping behavior further. Added\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-228-      2026-07-24: the retained text-cache workload now runs Latin/LTR,\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-229-      Arabic/RTL, Japanese/CJK LTR, and Devanagari/LTR cases, asserting cold\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-230-      shaping misses and warm cache reuse independently for every case.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-231-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-232-Full history, benchmark baselines, and rejected experiments live in\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-233-`.planning/performance/performance-log.md`; section letters (A–V) below\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-234-reference it. The historical subsystem map is\n--\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-659-      `widget_tree_build_end_to_end_benchmark`: 0.443–0.449ms per build before\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-660-      versus 0.416–0.424ms after (1.06x), and style resolution fell from 45% to\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-661-      39% of the build in `perf`. Cumulatively with the interned attribute map\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-662-      above, three interleaved pairs measured 0.504–0.511ms per build before\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-663-      both checkpoints versus 0.417–0.428ms after (1.18–1.22x).\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-664-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-665-      Added 2026-07-28: ordinary no-diagnostic theme-default lowering now\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-666-      survives fresh `StyleResolver` construction. `Theme` carries a monotonic\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:667:      style revision; clones with identical contents retain it, while mutable\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-668-      access to tokens, defaults, or module contributions advances it before\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-669-      exposing the data.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:670:      Resolvers share a bounded thread-local cache keyed by that revision,\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-671-      `(module_id, tag)`, and an exact collision-checked prop snapshot, so\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-672-      identical component instances share lowering while different `prop(...)`\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-673-      values remain isolated. Correctness coverage proves cross-resolver\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-674-      sharing, mutation invalidation, and prop-map isolation. Across three\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-675-      release runs of 100,000 fresh prop-bearing resolvers, repeated lowering\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:676:      took 125.7–128.8ms versus 18.83–20.35ms through the revision cache\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-677-      (6.18–6.84x); the relative speedup is checked by the canonical\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-678-      performance gate. The representative 456-node tree build measured\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-679-      0.390–0.397ms after this checkpoint versus 0.416–0.424ms before it\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-680-      (1.05–1.09x end to end). Typed property values and one-time token lowering\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-681-      remain open. Added 2026-07-28: indexed stylesheet declarations and\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-682-      theme-default maps now pre-lower static literals into typed colors,\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-683-      numbers, edges, corners, and dimensions. Applying those common values\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-684-      writes directly to `ComputedStyle`; `var()`/`prop()` values and all\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-685-      diagnostics deliberately retain the dynamic string path. Theme-default\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:686:      declaration arrays are shared by immutable theme revision and default-map\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-687-      identity, avoiding repeated temporary `Declaration` construction during\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-688-      cold resolver setup. Parity coverage compares typed application with the\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-689-      former string lowering across geometry, typography, color, and dimension\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:690:      properties; cache coverage proves reuse and revision invalidation. A\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-691-      release measurement and canonical gate remain pending because the local\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-692-      Rust linker wrapper is unavailable.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-693-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-694-- [x] Typed template-expression attribute storage (A). Internal evaluation was\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-695-      already typed, but results still stringified into attributes. Progress\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-696-      2026-07-15: boolean, nil, number, string, and compound JSON values remain\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-697-      typed through expression evaluation; attribute-boundary stringification\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-698-      is still the remaining step. Added 2026-07-25: `accessibility_for_element`\n--\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1212-      dispatches for up to `SURFACE_CONFIGURE_WAIT_DEADLINE` (500ms) inside\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1213-      presentation. One unconfigured surface can therefore stall every surface\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1214-      on the shell thread. Retain the pending frame, return a typed not-ready\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1215-      result, and wake/retry on configure; track the deadline in scheduler\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1216-      state for diagnostics instead of sleeping in `present`.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1217-- [ ] **P2 — Batch Wayland commits and event-queue progress per shell frame.**\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1218-      The current per-surface present path dispatches/flushes the queue, so\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1219-      multi-surface frames repeat connection work and obstruct the planned\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md:1220:      parallel paint/present phase split. Add a frame transaction or\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1221-      `present_many` boundary that prepares and commits all ready surfaces,\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1222-      then flushes once while preserving per-surface failure isolation.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1223-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1224-#### 10. Shell orchestrator, threading, and startup\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1225-\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1226-Trace: installed graph/discovery → parallel frontend compilation/catalog →\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1227-surface registration → frame prepare/layout/paint/present → live graph changes.\n.planning/log/backlog-archive-2026-07-28.md-1228-\n--\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-1-# Section 5 — Localization / i18n: improvement audit\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-2-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-3-**Audited:** 2026-08-19\n.planning/log/sec