ning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-55-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-56-## Confirmed findings\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-57-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-58-### 1. Critical — module-scoped translations leak through a global pool\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-59-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-60-`LocaleEngine::load_module_translations` stores a catalog under its module ID\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-61-and then also merges it into `translations`\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:62:(`crates/core/foundation/locale/src/lib.rs:70`). Both\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-63-`translate_for_module` and `effective_translations_for_module` fall back to\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-64-that pool (`:94` and `:109`). The last loaded module silently wins duplicate\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-65-global keys.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-66-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-67-Template evaluation is less safe still: `LocaleBoundState` has no module ID and\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-68-calls global `translate` (`crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/state.rs:412`).\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-69-A key missing from one module can therefore render text owned by an unrelated\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-70-module, with output depending on graph/catalog load order. This violates the\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-71-specification's primary isolation rule and lets an untrusted module spoof text\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-72-inside another module.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-73-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-74-**Improve it:** remove implicit global fallback. Every lookup must carry an\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-75-owning module or an explicitly named interface/core catalog domain. Build a\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-76-module-scoped translator from deterministic layers and use it for templates,\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-77-scripts, manifests, props, debug data, and generated settings UI.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-78-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:79:### 2. Critical — locale selection and fallback semantics are incorrect\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-80-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:81:`set_locale` inserts a new string at the front of the existing fallback vector\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:82:and deduplicates it (`crates/core/foundation/locale/src/lib.rs:56`). Old active\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:83:locales remain as accidental fallbacks. Constructors create only an exact\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-84-active/fallback pair (`:23` and `:33`): there is no BCP 47 validation,\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-85-canonicalization, or region/script parent derivation, so `sk-SK` does not find\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-86-a `sk` catalog.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-87-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:88:Components receive only `locale.current()` and mutate their own accumulated\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-89-chain (`crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/shell_component/mod.rs:1117`).\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:90:Changing `fallback_locale` can consequently leave component chains different\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-91-from the shell. Module `mesh.i18n.defaultLocale` is not carried in graph catalog\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-92-records and cannot serve as the required terminal per-module fallback\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-93-(`shell/discovery.rs:859`).\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-94-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-95-**Improve it:** define an immutable, normalized `LocaleSelection` containing\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:96:active tag, explicit/derived chain, direction, and revision. Replace rather\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-97-than mutate the chain, append each module's declared default only for that\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-98-module, and deliver the complete selection to every consumer.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-99-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-100-### 3. Critical — a plural value rejects its entire otherwise-valid catalog\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-101-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-102-`TranslationSet.messages` is `HashMap<String, String>`\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:103:(`crates/core/foundation/locale/src/lib.rs:7`), and surface mounting parses the\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-104-whole JSON file into the same type\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-105-(`crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/runtime.rs:248`). A specification-valid\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-106-`_plural` object makes deserialization fail and the loader skips every string\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-107-in that file. The only interpolation implementation is an unused, global-only\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-108-`translate_with`; Luau exposes only `t(key)`\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-109-(`crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/runtime/helpers.rs:125`).\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-110-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-111-**Improve it:** compile bounded typed catalog entries independently: messages,\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-112-CLDR plural/select variants, and checked placeholders. Invalid entries should\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-113-produce source-located diagnostics without discarding valid siblings. Expose\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-114-one module-aware interpolation/plural/number/date/duration formatter to every\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-115-consumption surface.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-116-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:117:### 4. High — catalog lifecycle is stale, repeated, and non-transactional\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-118-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-119-Every surface synchronously reads and parses every graph catalog during mount\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-120-(`crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/shell_component/mod.rs:79` and\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-121-`shell/component/runtime.rs:248`). Existing surfaces retain those private maps.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-122-The watcher includes settings, theme, and component source paths but no catalog\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-123-files (`crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/mod.rs:443`). Graph changes and\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-124-profile switches attach a new path vector only to newly constructed surfaces;\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-125-retained surfaces keep the old set (`shell/profile.rs:520` and `:855`).\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-126-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md:127:Settings/profile locale changes reconstruct only the shell engine, which has no\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-128-catalogs, then ask each component to reinterpret its existing maps\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-129-(`shell/runtime/theme.rs:395` and `shell/profile.rs:801`). An unreadable or\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-130-malformed catalog is only a warning and a candidate can commit with a partial\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-131-translation set.\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-132-\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-133-**Improve it:** load, parse, validate, and fingerprint graph-authorized inputs\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-134-once into an immutable `CatalogSnapshot`. Startup, graph changes, profile\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-135-switching, selection changes, and file reload should prepare one complete\n.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md-136-candidate, atomically commit its generation, and retain the last-known-good\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
