{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md | sed -n '130,185p'; nl -ba .planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md | sed -n '235,325p'\"","aggregated_output":"   130\tmalformed catalog is only a warning and a candidate can commit with a partial\n   131\ttranslation set.\n   132\t\n   133\t**Improve it:** load, parse, validate, and fingerprint graph-authorized inputs\n   134\tonce into an immutable `CatalogSnapshot`. Startup, graph changes, profile\n   135\tswitching, selection changes, and file reload should prepare one complete\n   136\tcandidate, atomically commit its generation, and retain the last-known-good\n   137\tsnapshot on failure. Rebind catalog watches after every committed graph.\n   138\t\n   139\t### 5. High — language-pack targeting, order, and provenance are absent\n   140\t\n   141\tThe specification marks language-pack layering as target, but the current data\n   142\tmodel cannot express it. `I18nContribution` contains only `id`, `locale`, and\n   143\t`path` (`crates/core/extension/module/src/package/module_manifest.rs:1353`).\n   144\tGraph indexing assigns the source module as the translation owner\n   145\t(`installed_graph/contributions.rs:193`); there is no target module, active pack\n   146\tchain, key-by-key precedence, or provenance.\n   147\t\n   148\t**Improve it:** add a validated target domain and deterministic ordered pack\n   149\tselection to the canonical graph/profile model. Compose user correction,\n   150\tordered packs, module-bundled locale, user fallback locales, and module default\n   151\texactly once, retaining the winning source for `which`, diagnostics, and debug\n   152\tinspection. Detect duplicate identities and ambiguous precedence before\n   153\tactivation.\n   154\t\n   155\t### 6. High — locale writes are non-durable and module defaults corrupt live state\n   156\t\n   157\t`apply_set_locale` trims only empty input, mutates the in-memory engine, and\n   158\tbroadcasts (`crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/theme.rs:455`). It does not\n   159\twrite the sparse settings/profile store, so restart or settings reload loses\n   160\tthe choice.\n   161\t\n   162\tSeparately, component settings interpret `i18n.default_locale` as a new active\n   163\tlocale (`shell/component/shell_component/mod.rs:1226`). That path neither\n   164\trefreshes the copied Luau translation maps nor runs the normal locale\n   165\tinvalidation flow, so a component engine, existing `t()` closure, and the shell\n   166\tcan disagree.\n   167\t\n   168\t**Improve it:** route manual, service, settings, and profile changes through one\n   169\trevision-checked durable selection transaction. Treat module default locale as\n   170\tmetadata in resolution, never as a component-local active-locale override.\n   171\t\n   172\t### 7. High — the Luau API and capability boundary contradict themselves\n   173\t\n   174\tRuntime documentation and LSP knowledge advertise\n   175\t`mesh.locale.translate(key, params)`, but `install_locale_api` installs only\n   176\t`current` and `set` (`crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/host_api.rs:14` and\n   177\t`context/runtime/host_api.rs:125`). A documented call therefore resolves to\n   178\t`nil`.\n   179\t\n   180\tThe direct host table is returned before interface-proxy resolution.\n   181\t`mesh.locale.current()` is installed without a `locale.read` check, and\n   182\t`require(\"mesh.i18n\")` returns the catalog helper before capability checks\n   183\t(`context/runtime/host_api.rs:125` and `:368`). A module without `locale.read`\n   184\tcan inspect locale state and probe effective keys, while `set` alone checks\n   185\t`locale.write`.\n   235\tThe component parser also accepts `<i18n>` as a known block, but `ComponentFile`\n   236\thas no corresponding field and `parse_component` discards it silently\n   237\t(`crates/core/ui/component/src/parser.rs:43` and `:82`).\n   238\t\n   239\t**Improve it:** drive LSP, CLI, extraction, and doctor output from the compiled\n   240\tcatalog/graph model. Either implement inline component catalogs with explicit\n   241\tprecedence or reject `<i18n>` with a migration diagnostic; never accept and\n   242\tdiscard author input.\n   243\t\n   244\t## Recommended target architecture\n   245\t\n   246\t```text\n   247\tInstalledModuleGraph + profile resource selection + sparse settings\n   248\t        │\n   249\t        ▼\n   250\tLocaleCoordinator::prepare(graph, selection, prior_snapshot)\n   251\t  ├─ validate/canonicalize BCP 47 active tag and fallback chain\n   252\t  ├─ open contained, bounded catalog sources\n   253\t  ├─ compile typed message/plural/select/placeholder entries\n   254\t  ├─ resolve target modules and ordered language-pack layers\n   255\t  └─ produce Arc<CatalogSnapshot>\n   256\t       { revision, selection, direction, module translators,\n   257\t         source provenance, structured diagnostics }\n   258\t        │\n   259\t        ▼\n   260\tatomic last-known-good commit + durable settings/profile revision\n   261\t        │\n   262\t        ├─ module-scoped Translator handles for template/Luau/manifest/props\n   263\t        ├─ one LocaleChanged event with selection + snapshot revision\n   264\t        ├─ dependency-aware component invalidation\n   265\t        └─ CLI/LSP/doctor inspection of the same graph and provenance\n   266\t```\n   267\t\n   268\tA useful feature beyond the current flow is an explicit locale policy\n   269\t(`manual`, `follow-system`, or per-profile). Portal/environment changes should\n   270\tenter the same prepare/persist/commit path, and direction should be snapshot\n   271\tmetadata so RTL layout changes cannot race translation changes.\n   272\t\n   273\t## Recommended implementation order\n   274\t\n   275\t1. Add regressions for cross-module leakage, stale fallback accumulation,\n   276\t   region/script fallback, plural-file rejection, non-durable selection,\n   277\t   retained-surface catalog staleness, API drift, and capability bypass.\n   278\t2. Freeze the canonical settings and contribution shapes; validate BCP 47,\n   279\t   nonempty/unique contribution identities, target modules, and pack order.\n   280\t3. Introduce typed catalog entries, per-entry diagnostics, limits, contained\n   281\t   source handles, and the immutable central snapshot.\n   282\t4. Remove the global pool and pass module-scoped translators through every\n   283\t   template, script, manifest, props, settings, and debug surface.\n   284\t5. Implement language-pack composition and per-module terminal defaults with\n   285\t   provenance and deterministic precedence.\n   286\t6. Route startup, settings/service writes, profile/graph changes, and catalog\n   287\t   reload through one durable prepare/commit coordinator.\n   288\t7. Align `mesh.i18n`, `mesh.locale`, service state/events, capabilities, LSP,\n   289\t   and CLI with one generated contract; add formatting and directionality.\n   290\t8. Add catalog watches, narrow invalidation by translator generation/key\n   291\t   dependencies, system-locale policy, extraction, missing-key, and `which`\n   292\t   tooling.\n   293\t\n   294\t## Required regression coverage\n   295\t\n   296\t- A module never resolves another module's catalog key, regardless of graph or\n   297\t  load order; explicit interface catalogs remain independently scoped.\n   298\t- BCP 47 tags normalize and derive parents (`zh-Hant-TW → zh-Hant → zh`), stale\n   299\t  active locales never remain in the chain, and each module default is terminal\n   300\t  only for that module.\n   301\t- String and plural/select entries coexist in one file; Slovak and English\n   302\t  categories, placeholder consistency, malformed sibling isolation, and size\n   303\t  limits are covered.\n   304\t- Two targeted packs shadow one module key in configured order; unrelated or\n   305\t  disabled packs do not participate; provenance identifies the winner.\n   306\t- Manual locale selection persists in the correct profile/settings scope and\n   307\t  survives restart; stale revisions and invalid tags do not mutate live state.\n   308\t- Catalog edits, graph enable/disable, and profile switches refresh retained and\n   309\t  new surfaces on one revision; an invalid candidate retains the old snapshot.\n   310\t- Catalog paths cannot escape through absolute, parent, or symlink traversal;\n   311\t  catalog bytes are read and parsed once per snapshot rather than once per\n   312\t  surface.\n   313\t- Templates, existing Luau `t()` handles, manifests, props, generated settings,\n   314\t  and debug data resolve the same module/revision and emit `!!key` plus one\n   315\t  structured miss diagnostic.\n   316\t- Runtime, service, documentation, and LSP APIs agree; `locale.read` and\n   317\t  `locale.write` denial is enforced consistently.\n   318\t- `<i18n>` is either compiled with documented precedence or rejected explicitly;\n   319\t  CLI/LSP locale discovery follows canonical graph contributions.\n   320\t\n   321\t## Verification\n   322\t\n   323\tFour Luna xhigh review passes reconstructed the flow, challenged its logical\n   324\torder and feature model, inspected concrete code defects, and audited catalog,\n   325\tfilesystem, capability, and tooling boundaries. No reviewer edited production\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
