{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' .planning/log/2026-08.md\"","aggregated_output":"# August 2026\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Align locale scripting ABI and capability gates\n\n`working tree` · area: localization runtime and authoring ABI\n\nThe canonical scripting surface is now consistent across the runtime, LSP,\nand specification: module-scoped translation is `import(\"mesh.i18n\", \"t\")`,\nwhile locale state exposes `mesh.locale.current()` and the write request\n`mesh.locale.set(locale)`. The runtime no longer injects locale reads or the\ni18n library without `locale.read`, exposes locale writes only with\n`locale.write`, and keeps the write operation checked at every call. LSP\ncompletion/hover knowledge and API documentation no longer advertise the\nremoved locale translation method.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale`\npassed (12 tests), `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-config --lib`\npassed (42 tests), and formatting/whitespace checks pass. New scripting and\nLSP regressions are present but cannot run because the pre-existing\n`InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229` stops compilation before\nthose crates.\n\n**Left open.** Centralized localized metadata and visible miss handling.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Commit locale writes through durable revision-checked settings/profile state\n\n`working tree` · area: locale persistence and profile transactions\n\nManual locale changes now prepare normalized BCP 47 selection and the complete\ngraph catalog before persistence. With an active profile, the sparse\n`shell.i18n` override is committed through the profile's expected revision;\nwithout one, the shared settings document uses the same revision-checked\natomic commit. Shared settings and profile mutation paths now advance their\nrevisions as well, preventing unrelated durable writers from being silently\noverwritten. The live locale engine, settings store, component invalidation,\nand service broadcast change only after the durable candidate succeeds.\nComponent-local `i18n.default_locale` no longer mutates the active locale.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-config --lib`\npassed (42 tests), `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale`\npassed (12 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and\n`git diff --check` pass. Shell/module tests remain blocked before the changed\ncrates by the pre-existing `InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Layer targeted language packs with provenance\n\n`working tree` · area: language-pack graph and locale resolution\n\nLanguage-pack contributions now declare an explicit target module. Active\nprofiles retain an ordered, duplicate-free language-pack chain, while legacy\ngraphs use a deterministic module-id order; non-pack resources cannot masquerade\nas language packs. Catalog preparation preserves pack layers ahead of\nmodule-bundled catalogs, applies each target module's declared default locale\nas a terminal fallback, and exposes the winning source provenance through the\nmodule translator. Duplicate target/locale entries within a pack and unavailable\ntargets are rejected or diagnosed before sources participate in lookup.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n(12 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and\n`git diff --check` pass. Module and shell tests remain blocked before their\ncrates by the pre-existing `InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Commit locale catalog snapshots with graph and profile state\n\n`working tree` · area: graph/profile/locale transactions\n\nGraph candidates now prepare every contributed catalog into one immutable,\nrevisioned `LocaleEngine` candidate before discovery, cached loading, module\nenable/disable, provider-selection, or backend-replacement commits. Profile\nswitch candidates retain the prepared locale engine until frontend and backend\nreadiness, and settings locale reloads reject invalid selection/catalog\ncandidates before changing the active settings snapshot. Shell-created\ncomponents consume that same catalog `Arc`; standalone component fixtures keep\ntheir local source-backed compatibility path. Any catalog read or JSON parse\nfailure leaves the previous graph, selection, and catalog snapshot active.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n(11 tests), `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed (23\ntests), `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-config --lib` passed (41\ntests), and formatting/whitespace checks pass. The shell regression is present\nbut cannot run because the pre-existing\n`InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229` stops compilation before\n`mesh-core-shell`.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Prepare graph locale catalogs before surface commit\n\n`working tree` · area: surface catalog lifecycle\n\nFrontend surfaces now compile graph catalogs into a fresh locale candidate and\nreplace their catalog Arc only after all catalog assets are readable. An asset\nread/parse failure retains the prior catalog snapshot while valid structured\nentries continue to produce per-entry diagnostics.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and\n`git diff --check` pass. The focused locale suite passed 9 tests before this\nshell-only wiring; workspace compilation remains blocked by pre-existing\nservice/module/scripting errors before the shell crate.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Establish immutable locale catalog snapshots\n\n`working tree` · area: catalog snapshot ownership\n\n`LocaleEngine` now stores catalogs behind a revisioned immutable\n`LocaleCatalogSnapshot` Arc. Catalog loads use copy-on-write preparation, and\ncallers can atomically replace the catalog pointer while readers retain the\nprevious last-known-good snapshot. The shell/graph/profile coordinator still\nneeds to adopt this seam; that remaining work stays open in the backlog.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n(9 tests), `git diff --check` passed. The final formatting check was retried\nafter the Nix daemon socket was temporarily unavailable; earlier focused\nformat checks pass for the same working tree.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Compile typed locale entries without sibling loss\n\n`working tree` · area: typed catalogs and shared message rendering\n\nLocale catalog loading now compiles bounded string, plural, and select entries\nindependently. Invalid keys, malformed placeholders, inconsistent variant\nplaceholders, unknown plural categories, and oversized entries produce\nper-entry diagnostics while valid siblings remain available. Rust translators\nshare interpolation and plural/select resolution, and Luau `t(key, values)`\nuses the same compiled entries. Graph catalog loading now accepts structured\nJSON instead of rejecting an entire file at the first plural object.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n(8 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff\n--check` pass. The scripting/shell workspace remains blocked by pre-existing\nclosure ownership and module graph compilation errors before shell compilation.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Normalize locale selection into revisioned snapshots\n\n`working tree` · area: locale selection and service state\n\nAdded immutable `LocaleSelection` snapshots with canonical BCP 47 casing,\nderived script/region parents, explicit terminal fallback, RTL/LTR direction,\nand monotonic revisions. Locale changes now replace the prior chain instead of\naccumulating stale locales; invalid runtime tags are rejected. The shell\npublishes the normalized chain, direction, and revision, and retained\ncomponents adopt the same selection snapshot.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n(7 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff\n--check` pass. Workspace compilation remains blocked by pre-existing errors in\nthe service, module, and scripting crates before shell compilation.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Replace global locale lookup with owner-scoped translators\n\n`working tree` · area: localization ownership and consumption\n\n`LocaleEngine` no longer merges module catalogs into a shared translation\npool. It now exposes explicit module and core translator handles; module\ntranslators resolve only their owner’s catalogs. Template variable stores,\nLuau i18n maps, manifest text, debug metadata, and generated composition prop\nsettings all use the corresponding owner-scoped handle. Existing keybind/debug\nfixtures were migrated to module-owned catalogs, and cross-module/core leakage\nis covered by locale tests.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n(4 tests), `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff\n--check` pass. The scripting/shell compile remains blocked by the pre-existing\n`InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Route theme mode policies through candidate preparation\n\n`working tree` · area: theme mode selection and settings\n\nTheme settings now support explicit `manual`, `follow_system`, and\n`scheduled` policies. A pure selector validates declared modes, matches system\ncolor-scheme metadata, resolves local clock schedules, and rejects malformed,\nunknown, or duplicate entries. Graph theme preparation and reload fingerprint\nchecks use that selector, so policy transitions enter the same candidate\ncomposition, invalidation, and revisioned event path as manual changes.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed\n(23 tests), `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-config --lib` passed\n(41 tests), and formatting/diff checks pass. The focused shell suite remains\nblocked by the pre-existing `InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Make active theme snapshots immutable and identities deterministic\n\n`working tree` · area: theme snapshot identity and catalog registration\n\nThemeEngine now keeps an `Arc` of the active immutable snapshot and refreshes it\nonly after controlled active-theme edits or replacement commits. The unrestricted\nmutable active-theme accessor was removed; duplicate, whitespace-ambiguous, and\nempty available-theme identities are rejected before registration, while graph\nregistration reports the rejection and continues safely.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed\n(21 tests); `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. The\nfocused shell suite remains blocked by the pre-existing\n`InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n\n## 2026-08-22 — Publish the authoritative rendered theme snapshot\n\n`working tree` · area: theme snapshot state and events\n\nThe shell now publishes the rendered theme snapshot as the sole `mesh.theme`\nstate source and declares shell-owned `ThemeChanged` and `TokenChanged`\ninterface events. Theme changes carry mode, color scheme, contrast, revision,\nthe complete effective token/provenance maps, and deterministic changed-token\nrecords; individual token events carry the same revision and winning-layer\nprovenance. Provider state cannot overwrite the rendered snapshot.\n\n**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-theme` passed\n(20 tests); `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. The\nfocused shell suite is blocked by a pre-existing compile error in\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229` (`InterfaceProvider`\ncannot be dereferenced).\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Retain last-known-good theme candidates\n\n`4d11e431` · area: theme/profile/reload transactions\n\nProfile switches prepare graph-selected theme sources before committing the\ncandidate runtime. Reload parsing and component invalidation failures now keep\nthe prior theme/watch snapshot and record `theme_reload_rejected`; successful\nprofile theme changes preserve the existing catalog while replacing only the\nprepared active snapshot.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Open theme selections through contained graph sources\n\n`73dcc5ad` · area: theme source security and selection\n\nTheme selection now accepts only graph-scoped catalog identities. Their mode\nsources open beneath the owning module root with no-follow directory/file\nhandles, bounded reads, regular-file checks, and UTF-8 validation; registration\nand reload use the same boundary. Legacy free-form selection paths are rejected\nby the shell control path.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Build the graph-authorized theme catalog\n\n`447d2b43` · area: theme catalog and module graph\n\nEnabled canonical theme contributions now form one deterministic catalog keyed\nby owner-scoped identity. Descriptors retain owner module, label, ordered modes,\nvalidated default mode, and a module-root-relative source handle. Runtime theme\nregistration consumes that catalog instead of scanning `config/themes`.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Commit signed module provenance verification\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
