{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc 'git diff -- crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs .planning/STATUS.md .planning/log/2026-08.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.planning/STATUS.md b/.planning/STATUS.md\nindex 382bb239..79220200 100644\n--- a/.planning/STATUS.md\n+++ b/.planning/STATUS.md\n@@ -4,14 +4,16 @@\n \n ## Now\n \n-The locale scripting ABI is aligned: `mesh.i18n.t` is the module-scoped read\n-surface, `mesh.locale.current` is the locale read surface, and\n-`mesh.locale.set` is the locale write surface. Runtime injection and\n-`require` enforce `locale.read`/`locale.write` independently, and LSP\n-knowledge matches the runtime.\n+Localized runtime misses now use the same owner/key/fallback/source/snapshot\n+resolution record as manifest metadata. Luau and template consumers render\n+`!!key`, enqueue structured observations, and shell diagnostics deduplicate\n+them by module/key; manifest fields retain their field path in the resolution.\n \n-The next open localization item is centralized localized metadata and visible\n-miss handling with owner, fallback, source, and snapshot revision. Config (42)\n-and locale (12) test suites pass; scripting/LSP/module/shell validation remains\n-blocked by the pre-existing `InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\n-`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\n+Graph-authorized locale catalogs now retain a module-root/relative-path source\n+handle. Reads reject traversal and symlink components, require regular files,\n+enforce a 2 MiB UTF-8 bound, and feed the immutable catalog snapshot without\n+free-form `read_to_string` paths.\n+\n+The same open localization item still needs catalog preparation and compilation\n+to run through a non-shell worker boundary. Locale (15) passes; shell\n+validation is blocked by the pre-existing module-package compile errors.\ndiff --git a/.planning/log/2026-08.md b/.planning/log/2026-08.md\nindex f4bf5504..cc325044 100644\n--- a/.planning/log/2026-08.md\n+++ b/.planning/log/2026-08.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,46 @@\n # August 2026\n \n+## 2026-08-22 — Contain graph catalogs with bounded no-follow handles\n+\n+`working tree` · area: localization catalog I/O\n+\n+Graph-authorized catalog sources now retain their owning module root and a\n+validated relative path instead of relying on a free-form joined pathname.\n+Catalog reads traverse the root and relative components with `O_NOFOLLOW`,\n+reject traversal/absolute components and non-regular files, cap input at 2 MiB,\n+and validate UTF-8 before JSON parsing. The immutable snapshot preparation path\n+uses this handle, while the previous last-known-good commit behavior remains\n+unchanged.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n+(15 tests), including escape, symlink, regular-file, UTF-8, and size-bound\n+regressions. Shell checking reached the existing module-package errors\n+(`ThemeModeMetadata`, `ShellProfile.revision`, and two inference failures) and\n+reported no new locale errors before that dependency stopped compilation.\n+\n+**Left open.** Move catalog reading/parsing/compilation behind a non-shell\n+worker boundary before removing this backlog item.\n+\n+## 2026-08-22 — Centralize runtime localized misses and metadata identity\n+\n+`working tree` · area: localization consumption and diagnostics\n+\n+Luau `mesh.i18n.t()` and template `t(...)` now resolve through one structured\n+missing-result path. Missing values remain visibly `!!key`, while the queued\n+record retains the owning module, key, fallback, field path, catalog source,\n+and snapshot revision for shell diagnostics. Manifest metadata uses the same\n+field-aware resolution record and shell diagnostics deduplicate active misses\n+by owner and key instead of emitting one generic runtime warning per render.\n+\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\n+(13 tests); the focused scripting miss regression passed; scripting library\n+check passed; formatting and `git diff --check` pass. The full scripting suite\n+still has one unrelated pre-existing service-ticket assertion failure, and\n+shell compilation remains blocked by existing module-package errors.\n+\n+**Left open.** Bounded no-follow catalog handles and off-thread catalog\n+compilation.\n+\n ## 2026-08-22 — Align locale scripting ABI and capability gates\n \n `working tree` · area: localization runtime and authoring ABI\ndiff --git a/crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs b/crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs\nindex 6646f733..0137e495 100644\n--- a/crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs\n+++ b/crates/core/shell/src/shell/discovery.rs\n@@ -25,10 +25,13 @@ fn load_installed_module_graph_candidate(\n \n pub(in crate::shell) fn graph_i18n_catalog_sources(\n     graph: &InstalledModuleGraph,\n-) -> (\n-    Vec<mesh_core_locale::CatalogSource>,\n-    HashMap<String, String>,\n-) {\n+) -> Result<\n+    (\n+        Vec<mesh_core_locale::CatalogSource>,\n+        HashMap<String, String>,\n+    ),\n+    String,\n+> {\n     let selected_packs = graph\n         .language_pack_chain()\n         .iter()\n@@ -53,16 +56,24 @@ pub(in crate::shell) fn graph_i18n_catalog_sources(\n \n     let mut sources = bundled\n         .into_iter()\n-        .filter_map(|catalog| {\n-            let module_dir = catalog.source.manifest_path.parent()?;\n-            Some(mesh_core_locale::CatalogSource::module(\n+        .map(|catalog| {\n+            let module_dir = catalog.source.manifest_path.parent().ok_or_else(|| {\n+                format!(\n+                    \"i18n catalog {} has no module root: {}\",\n+                    catalog.id,\n+                    catalog.source.manifest_path.display()\n+                )\n+            })?;\n+            mesh_core_locale::CatalogSource::module_from_root(\n                 catalog.module_id.clone(),\n                 catalog.id.clone(),\n                 catalog.locale.clone(),\n-                module_dir.join(&catalog.path),\n-            ))\n+                module_dir.to_path_buf(),\n+                &catalog.path,\n+            )\n+            .map_err(|reason| format!(\"invalid i18n catalog {}: {reason}\", catalog.id))\n         })\n-        .collect::<Vec<_>>();\n+        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;\n \n     for pack_module_id in graph.language_pack_chain() {\n         let mut pack_catalogs = graph\n@@ -79,16 +90,24 @@ pub(in crate::shell) fn graph_i18n_catalog_sources(\n             .collect::<Vec<_>>();\n         pack_catalogs.sort_by(|left, right| left.id.cmp(&right.id));\n         for catalog in pack_catalogs {\n-            let Some(module_dir) = catalog.source.manifest_path.parent() else {\n-                continue;\n-            };\n-            sources.push(mesh_core_locale::CatalogSource::language_pack(\n-                catalog.module_id.clone(),\n-                catalog.target_module_id.clone(),\n-                catalog.id.clone(),\n-                catalog.locale.clone(),\n-                module_dir.join(&catalog.path),\n-            ));\n+            let module_dir = catalog.source.manifest_path.parent().ok_or_else(|| {\n+                format!(\n+                    \"i18n catalog {} has no module root: {}\",\n+                    catalog.id,\n+                    catalog.source.manifest_path.display()\n+                )\n+            })?;\n+            sources.push(\n+                mesh_core_locale::CatalogSource::language_pack_from_root(\n+                    catalog.module_id.clone(),\n+                    catalog.target_module_id.clone(),\n+                    catalog.id.clone(),\n+                    catalog.locale.clone(),\n+                    module_dir.to_path_buf(),\n+                    &catalog.path,\n+                )\n+                .map_err(|reason| format!(\"invalid i18n catalog {}: {reason}\", catalog.id))?,\n+            );\n         }\n     }\n \n@@ -106,7 +125,7 @@ pub(in crate::shell) fn graph_i18n_catalog_sources(\n                 .map(|locale| (module.id.clone(), locale))\n         })\n         .collect();\n-    (sources, defaults)\n+    Ok((sources, defaults))\n }\n \n fn log_locale_catalog_diagnostics(diagnostics: &[mesh_core_locale::CatalogSourceDiagnostics]) {\n@@ -893,7 +912,8 @@ impl Shell {\n         graph: &InstalledModuleGraph,\n     ) -> Result<LocaleEngine, ShellRunError> {\n         let mut candidate = self.locale.clone();\n-        let (sources, defaults) = graph_i18n_catalog_sources(graph);\n+        let (sources, defaults) =\n+            graph_i18n_catalog_sources(graph).map_err(ShellRunError::LocaleCatalog)?;\n         let prepared = candidate\n             .prepare_catalog_snapshot(&sources, &defaults)\n             .map_err(|error| ShellRunError::LocaleCatalog(error.to_string()))?;\n@@ -908,7 +928,8 @@ impl Shell {\n         graph: &InstalledModuleGraph,\n     ) -> Result<LocaleEngine, ShellRunError> {\n         let mut candidate = self.prepare_locale_selection_for_settings(settings)?;\n-        let (sources, defaults) = graph_i18n_catalog_sources(graph);\n+        let (sources, defaults) =\n+            graph_i18n_catalog_sources(graph).map_err(ShellRunError::LocaleCatalog)?;\n         let prepared = candidate\n             .prepare_catalog_snapshot(&sources, &defaults)\n             .map_err(|error| ShellRunError::LocaleCatalog(error.to_string()))?;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
