{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \"tail -60 .planning/log/2026-08.md; rg -n \\\"Open bounded catalogs\\\" docs/BACKLOG.md; sed -n '1,40p' .planning/STATUS.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n`working tree` · area: theme cascade and graph-selected snapshots\n\nThe runtime now prepares a four-layer theme snapshot: recovery defaults,\nselected graph theme pack/mode, enabled frontend-owned contributions scoped to\ntheir module IDs, and sparse shell user token overrides. The theme engine keeps\nper-value provenance for the winning layer, validates scalar overrides and\nmodule targets, and profile/settings/reload paths use the same graph composer.\nTheme settings now accept an optional mode and scalar token map.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable. No performance claim is made.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Share restricted CSS selectors between components and themes\n\n`working tree` · area: CSS parsing, theme lowering, and style matching\n\nThe restricted selector AST and parser now live in the theme foundation and\nare reused by component style lowering. Theme CSS retains supported compound,\nclass, ID, and state rules as executable declarations; the element resolver\nmatches global and module-scoped theme rules through the same matcher as local\ncomponent styles. Theme declaration scanning now respects quotes/functions and\nrejects unterminated comments, malformed values, unmatched syntax, and trailing\nCSS instead of silently storing dead rules.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable. No performance claim is made.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Persist and fingerprint theme selections\n\n`working tree` · area: theme persistence, reload observation, and revisions\n\nTheme selection now persists the active graph identity and clears stale mode\nstate through the settings store. Theme watch state carries a stable content\nfingerprint, selected mode, and snapshot revision; graph sources fingerprint\nthrough their contained safe handle. Reload checks fingerprints even when file\nmtimes are unchanged and keeps polling after selection changes so a new source\ndirectory is observable despite the startup inotify set. Theme service state\npublishes the mode, fingerprint, and revision with the rendered selection.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable. No performance claim is made.\n\n## 2026-08-21 — Unify theme and component keyframes and token dependencies\n\n`Theme` now resolves transitive `var(--...)` token aliases against one\nimmutable snapshot, preserves scalar alias types, supports CSS fallbacks, and\nreports missing, malformed, and cyclic dependency paths. The element resolver\nuses that result for cached style values and carries computed custom\nproperties through initial construction, full restyles, targeted restyles, and\ncomponent rendering. Theme `@keyframes` are converted into the same runtime\nstop representation as component keyframes, with inherited custom properties\navailable while lowering each stop.\n\nVerification: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check` pass. Focused\nCargo tests remain blocked because the local registry cache lacks `sha2` and\nnetwork access is unavailable. No performance claim is made.\n56:- [ ] Open bounded catalogs through contained no-follow source handles and compile them off the shell thread.\n# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-08-22\n\n## Now\n\nLocalized runtime misses now use the same owner/key/fallback/source/snapshot\nresolution record as manifest metadata. Luau and template consumers render\n`!!key`, enqueue structured observations, and shell diagnostics deduplicate\nthem by module/key; manifest fields retain their field path in the resolution.\n\nGraph-authorized locale catalogs now retain a module-root/relative-path source\nhandle. Reads reject traversal and symlink components, require regular files,\nenforce a 2 MiB UTF-8 bound, and feed the immutable catalog snapshot without\nfree-form `read_to_string` paths.\n\nThe same open localization item still needs catalog preparation and compilation\nto run through a non-shell worker boundary. Locale (15) passes; shell\nvalidation is blocked by the pre-existing module-package compile errors.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
