bels in `<props>` are\\n`LocalizedText` resolved the same way ([03 §3](03-components.md)). The\\ninstalled graph sc fallback, source, and snapshot revision. Config (42)\\n-and locale (12) test suites pass; scripting/LSP/module/shell validation remains\\n-blocked by the pre-existing `InterfaceProvider` dereference error at\\n-`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229`.\\n+The next open localization item is bounded catalog opening and off-thread\\n+compilation. Locale (13) and the focused scripting regression pass. Full\\n+scripting still has one unrelated service-ticket assertion failure; shell\\n+validation is blocked by pre-existing module-package compile errors after the\\n+stale service dereference was corrected.\\ndiff --git a/.planning/log/2026-08.md b/.planning/log/2026-08.md\\nindex f4bf5504..0fcea9f5 100644\\n--- a/.planning/log/2026-08.md\\n+++ b/.planning/log/2026-08.md\\n@@ -1,5 +1,25 @@\\n # August 2026\\n \\n+## 2026-08-22 — Centralize runtime localized misses and metadata identity\\n+\\n+`working tree` · area: localization consumption and diagnostics\\n+\\n+Luau `mesh.i18n.t()` and template `t(...)` now resolve through one structured\\n+missing-result path. Missing values remain visibly `!!key`, while the queued\\n+record retains the owning module, key, fallback, field path, catalog source,\\n+and snapshot revision for shell diagnostics. Manifest metadata uses the same\\n+field-aware resolution record and shell diagnostics deduplicate active misses\\n+by owner and key instead of emitting one generic runtime warning per render.\\n+\\n+**Verification.** `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` passed\\n+(13 tests); the focused scripting miss regression passed; scripting library\\n+check passed; formatting and `git diff --check` pass. The full scripting suite\\n+still has one unrelated pre-existing service-ticket assertion failure, and\\n+shell compilation remains blocked by existing module-package errors.\\n+\\n+**Left open.** Bou