rv\\\\n/nix/store/7av3syv27qsqr40vm96c6i14zdsibcmr-crate-sha2-0.10.8.tar.gz.drv\\\\n/nix/store/6aw5x69pa5s9scwsk8y4lg2vjipgz3m7-sha2-0.10.8.drv\\\\n/nix/store/z0swsfcs9g5mdfrnd946vfg608vwd4ly-crate-sha2-0.10.9.tar.gz.drv\\\\n/nix/store/k0djjbg7avigfra9mz5dxw1rlgnb538w-sha2-0.10.9.drv\\\\n/nix/store/zkc2ils2svzp8d1fn47k7pcl6sk0ykia-cryptohash-sha256-0.11.102.1-r6.cabal.drv\\\\n/nix/store/xpgvg14glsix3znxypi1925dkz2jmmia-cryptohash-sha256-0.11.102.1.tar.gz.drv\\\\n/nix/store/mb8wl7v04mk1p22r696m5v0yq5wgi6zf-cryptohash-sha256-0.11.102.1.drv\\\\n/nix/store/yybjiv6d8vz7qrsm10ymf715pfy63jm8-cryptohash-sha256-0.11.102.1-r6.cabal.drv\\\\n/nix/store/0sjw784zmzlk47sp168mjv4pk35grlj0-cryptohash-sha256-0.11.102.1.tar.gz.drv\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_112\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"find /nix/store -maxdepth 1 -type d \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\( -name '*sha2-0.10.8*' -o -name '*sha2-0.10.9*' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\) -print 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,80p'; find /nix/store -maxdepth 1 -type d -name '*rustc*' -print 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,20p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_112\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"find /nix/store -maxdepth 1 -type d \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\( -name '*sha2-0.10.8*' -o -name '*sha2-0.10.9*' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\) -print 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,80p'; find /nix/store -maxdepth 1 -type d -name '*rustc*' -print 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,20p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_113\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implemented and closed the highest-priority bacfor decoded assets, fonts, glyphs, text, Skia, PixelBuffer, and SHM allocations.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Introduce a typed frame paint plan with immutable inputs, topology, transforms, effect regions, replay spans, and exact logical/device damage.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 13. Surface policy and configuration\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/13-surface-policy-and-configuration/improvements.md)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Enforce the author-only `promotable` guard for settings, IPC, and live role changes.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Remove or formally protect `promotable` from user-overridable/ejected settings.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Validate manifest surface enums and role constraints with canonical parsers before graph resolution.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Include blur and window decorations in semantic presentation change detection.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Route settings-driven role reloads through the same transactional transition supervisor as explicit promotion.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Share role-field metadata across manifest diagnostics, settings validation, ejection, and protocol lowering.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Preserve localization identity and distinguish effective values from overrides during configuration ejection.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Use typed unmeasured/content/surface/wire extents at the shell/presentation boundary.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Replace split surface field lists with a revisioned semantic policy diff and generation.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Build the policy compiler producing declared contracts, effective snapshots, and typed transition plans.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 14. Wayland platform and presentation\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/14-wayland-platform-and-presentation/improvements.md)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Return typed create/configure/present/lost outcomes, cache only accepted generations, and retain damage for missing surfaces.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Route close, dismiss, parent destruction, role replacement, and connection loss through one idempotent teardown supervisor.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Replace incomplete presentation hashes and warm region caches with typed semantic diffs and object/configure/frame generations.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Preserve click-grab seat and serial identity through input normalization, popup requests, and one-shot configuration.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Gate popup reposition by negotiated protocol version and validate popup role, parent, identity, and reparenting.\\\\\\\\n- [ ] Use one authoritative logical extent for paint, buffer validation, viewport, regions, attach, and queries.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncodex-loop.log:394:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'^'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\- \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\]' docs/BACKLOG.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"47:- [ ] Replace shared Luau service globals with generation-stamped, Rust-owned, capability-filtered context state.\\\\\\\\n48:- [ ] Make service methods correlated awaitable transactions with call IDs, deadlines, cancellation, and terminal outcomes.\\\\\\\\n49:- [ ] Make optimistic state writes settle or roll back transactionally without overriding newer writes.\\\\\\\\n50:- [ ] Compile and enforce explicit read, event-subscription, and per-method operation policy at every service boundary.\\\\\\\\n51:- [ ] Replace additive registry mutation with one immutable generation-stamped resolved service catalog.\\\\\\\\n52:- [ ] Compile recursive named/array/optional/result schemas and enforce them for state, events, inputs, and outputs.\\\\\\\\n53:- [ ] Prepare provider output and commit provider selection only after validated readiness and initial state.\\\\\\\\n54:- [ ] Deliver generation-stamped availability transitions and reject stale state, event, and result messages.\\\\\\\\n55:- [ ] Diff executable consumer/provider contracts in both directions, including external candidate contracts and behavioral annotations.\\\\\\\\n56:- [ ] Canonicalize contract identities and make graph, runtime, LSP, codegen, docs, and diagnostics consume one compiled artifact.\\\\\\\\n57:- [ ] Remove the transitional service registry after remaining callers migrate to the generation-stamped catalog.\\\\\\\\n58:- [ ] Introduce an immutable compiled contract containing schemas, operation policy, fingerprints, and declaration provenance.\\\\\\\\n59:- [ ] Generate Luau consumer types, provider stubs, mocks, and contract documentation from compiled contracts.\\\\\\\\n60:- [ ] Model optional service feature groups explicitly and negotiate them per provider, or remove the unsupported claim.\\\\\\\\n61:- [ ] Make consumer/provider compatibility classifications independently expressible rather than using one undirected label.\\\\\\\\n62:- [ ] Use one call transaction model for awaitable results, cancellation, deadlines, coalescing, tracing, and optimistic rollback.\\\\\\\\n68:- [ ] Build the theme catalog only from graph-authorized descriptors with scoped ownership, modes, and contained source handles.\\\\\\\\n69:- [ ] Resolve theme selections through catalog identities with symlink-safe, bounded, UTF-8-checked source opening.\\\\\\\\n70:- [ ] Prepare and atomically commit theme/profile/reload candidates while retaining the last-known-good snapshot on failure.\\\\\\\\n71:- [ ] Implement the base, selected pack/mode, owned module contribution, and sparse user override cascade with provenance.\\\\\\\\n72:- [ ] Make theme selection durable, fingerprinted, watchable, and revision-consistent across settings/profile changes.\\\\\\\\n73:- [ ] Share a restricted CSS parser/lowering and selector matcher between component and theme styles.\\\\\\\\n74:- [ ] Share keyframes across theme and component styles and resolve token dependencies, cycles, and inherited custom properties.\\\\\\\\n75:- [ ] Make the rendered theme snapshot authoritative for mode, color scheme, contrast, tokens, provenance, and revisioned events.\\\\\\\\n76:- [ ] Make theme snapshots immutable and reject duplicate or ambiguous identities for deterministic caching.\\\\\\\\n77:- [ ] Add explicit manual, follow-system, and scheduled theme mode policies through the same transaction coordinator.\\\\\\\\n83:- [ ] Replace the global translation pool with owner-scoped translators for templates, scripts, manifests, props, debug data, and settings UI.\\\\\\\\n84:- [ ] Implement an immutable normalized locale selection with BCP 47 parents, direction, complete fallback chain, and revision.\\\\\\\\n85:- [ ] Compile bounded typed message/plural/select entries independently with checked placeholders and shared formatting.\\\\\\\\n86:- [ ] Build one immutable catalog snapshot with atomic graph/profile/selection/reload commits and last-known-good recovery.\\\\\\\\n87:- [ ] Add targeted ordered language-pack chains, per-module defaults, winning-source provenance, and duplicate precedence checks.\\\\\\\\n88:- [ ] Route locale changes through one durable revision-checked settings/profile transaction.\\\\\\\\n89:- [ ] Align `mesh.i18n`, `mesh.locale`, runtime/LSP ABI, and read/write capability enforcement.\\\\\\\\n90:- [ ] Centralize localized metadata and visible miss handling with owner, fallback, source, and snapshot revision.\\\\\\\\n91:- [ ] Open bounded catalogs through contained no-follow source handles and compile them off the shell thread.\\\\\\\\n92:- [ ] Drive locale CLI/LSP/extraction/doctor tooling from the canonical graph, and implement or explicitly reject `<i18n>` blocks.\\\\\\\\n93:- [ ] Add manual, follow-system, and per-profile locale policies through the same prepare/persist/commit path.\\\\\\\\n99:- [ ] Build icon and font resources only from the prepared graph/profile and a