her settings/profile mutation paths advance through revision-checked writes\n  so they cannot silently invalidate locale candidates.\n- Component `i18n.default_locale` is metadata only; it no longer forks the\n  active locale in a component.\n- `mesh.i18n.t` is the module-scoped read surface; `mesh.locale.current` and\n  `mesh.locale.set` are independently gated by `locale.read` and\n  `locale.write`. Runtime and LSP knowledge no longer advertise the removed\n  locale translation method.\n- The locale backlog item was removed from `docs/BACKLOG.md` and recorded in\n  `.planning/log/2026-08.md`; `.planning/STATUS.md` was shortened and updated.\n\n## Repository and git state\n\n- Repository: `/home/kolby/projects/mesh`.\n- All changes are uncommitted on `main`; no commit was created.\n- The worktree is intentionally dirty from the preceding theme/localization\n  work and this increment. Preserve all unrelated changes.\n- Current dirty files include `.codex-continuation.md`, planning/docs files,\n  `Cargo.lock`, `codex-loop.log`, foundation config/locale/theme crates,\n  module graph/profile files and tests, scripting runtime files, and shell\n  discovery/profile/package/component/runtime/test files.\n\n## Files changed in this increment\n\n- `crates/core/foundation/config/src/lib.rs`\n- `crates/core/foundation/config/src/settings.rs`\n- `crates/core/extension/module/src/package/profile.rs`\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/runtime/theme.rs`\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/profile.rs`\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/package.rs`\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/module_config.rs`\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/component/shell_component/mod.rs`\n- `crates/core/shell/src/shell/tests/theme.rs`\n- `crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/context/tests/imports.rs`\n- `crates/core/runtime/scripting/src/host_api.rs`\n- `crates/tools/lsp/src/analyzer/mod.rs`\n- `crates/tools/lsp/src/analyzer/script.rs`\n- `crates/tools/lsp/src/knowledge/mesh_api.rs`\n- `docs/BACKLOG.md`, `docs/spec/07-i18n.md`, `.planning/STATUS.md`, and this\n  handoff; `.planning/log/2026-08.md` has the dated record.\n\n## Architectural decisions\n\n- Durable settings revision is stored as top-level `revision`; legacy/missing\n  documents start at zero.\n- Durable profile revision is stored as `revision` in `ShellProfile`; zero is\n  omitted when serializing legacy-compatible profiles.\n- Locale writes are prepare → durable expected-revision commit → live runtime\n  commit. Invalid catalogs, invalid locale tags, persistence failures, or stale\n  revisions retain the current live snapshot.\n- An active profile owns the locale override; without an active profile, the\n  shared settings document owns it. Profile locale preparation also checks the\n  shared settings revision so fallback changes cannot race the profile write.\n- Module defaults participate only in catalog fallback resolution, never as\n  component-local active-locale state.\n\n## Tests and results\n\nPassed:\n\n- `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-config --lib` — 42 tests.\n- `nix develop --command cargo test -p mesh-core-locale` — 12 tests.\n- `nix develop --command cargo fmt --all -- --check`.\n- `git diff --check`.\n\nBlocked: scripting, LSP, module, and shell checks/tests stop before the changed\ncrates at the pre-existing compile error:\n`crates/core/extension/service/src/interface.rs:229` —\n`InterfaceProvider` cannot be dereferenced. Do not claim those suites passed.\n\n## Unresolved problems\n\n- The next localization item is centralized localized metadata and visible miss\n  handling with owner, fallback, source, and snapshot revision.\n- Later localization items remain: centralized visible miss/metadata handling,\n  contained bounded catalog opening and off-thread compilation, canonical\n  CLI/LSP/extraction/doctor tooling, and locale policies.\n- Broader validation remains blocked by the known service compile error.\n\n## Exact next steps\n\n1. Re-read the current localization audit, `docs/spec/07-i18n.md`, and the\n   localized metadata/miss paths in graph diagnostics, manifest resolution,\n[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/03-service-contracts/improvements.md)\n\n\n### 4. Themes\n\n[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/04-themes/improvements.md)\n\n### 5. Localization and i18n\n\n[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/05-localization-i18n/improvements.md)\n\n- [ ] Drive locale CLI/LSP/extraction/doctor tooling from the canonical graph, and implement or explicitly reject `<i18n>` blocks.\n- [ ] Add manual, follow-system, and per-profile locale policies through the same prepare/persist/commit path.\n\n### 6. Host resources and icon packs\n\n[Audit](../.planning/log/sections/06-host-resources-and-icon-packs/improvements.md)\n\n- [ ] Build icon and font resources only from the prepared graph/profile and atomically retain the last-known-good resource snapshot.\n- [ ] Preserve declared pack order and reject duplicate canonical IDs, aliases, and ambiguous ownership deterministically.\n- [ ] Open module resource assets through contained, no-follow, bounded handles.\n# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-08-22\n\n## Now\n\nLocalized runtime misses now use the same owner/key/fallback/source/snapshot\nresolution record as manifest metadata. Luau and template consumers render\n`!!key`, enqueue structured observations, and shell diagnostics deduplicate\nthem by module/key; manifest fields retain their field path in the resolution.\n\nGraph-authorized locale catalogs retain a module-root/relative-path source\nhandle. Reads reject traversal and symlink components, require regular files,\nenforce a 2 MiB UTF-8 bound, and feed immutable snapshot preparation through a\nnamed worker thread instead of compiling on the shell thread.\n\nThe next open localization item is canonical-graph locale CLI/LSP/extraction/\ndoctor tooling and the explicit `<i18n>` block policy. Locale (16) passes; shell\nvalidation remains blocked by the pre-existing module-package compile errors.\n","exit_code":0,"st